WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.960
[fan 1, in Spanish] He lied to Barça fans.

2
00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.160
[fan 2, in Spanish]
He broke our hearts. He's gonna pay.

3
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.640
[fan 3, in Spanish]
He's a mercenary. He can go to hell.

4
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:21.360
-[emergency vehicle siren wails]
-[air horn booms]

5
00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:23.440
[people chanting]

6
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.760
[man, chanting] Barça! Barça!

7
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.600
[commentator 1, in Spanish]
Welcome to football in its purest form.

8
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:41.960
One of world football's great derbies.

9
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.640
A NETFLIX DOCUMENTARY

10
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.560
[crowd roaring]

11
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.640
[commentator 2, in English]
Barcelona vs Real Madrid.

12
00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:55.400
Catalonia versus Spain.

13
00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.600
But tonight, it is all about one man.

14
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.280
[commentator 4, in Portuguese]
It's a hostile reception,

15
00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:03.640
especially for Luís Figo.

16
00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.680
Traitor, mercenary, Judas.

17
00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.080
That's what the Barcelona fans
are calling him,

18
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.840
even though
he was once a hero in Catalonia.

19
00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.560
[commentator 5, in Spanish] Watch out!
This could explode at any moment!

20
00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.200
CATALONIA DOESN'T FORGET. JUDA$!!

21
00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.560
[commentator 1, in Spanish]
They're throwing everything at Luís Figo.

22
00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.360
Everything.

23
00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.400
[Barça fans yelling expletives in Spanish]

24
00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:43.440
[commentator 1, in Spanish] It's over.
The game's about to be suspended.

25
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.440
[continues commentating]

26
00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.480
[commentator 2, in English]
Seems like only yesterday

27
00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.120
that Luís Figo was worshipped
in this stadium.

28
00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.280
How on earth did it end up like this?

29
00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.280
[Barça fans jeering at Figo]

30
00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:10.760
[Figo] So many people
think they know the story.

31
00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.880
But I'm the one that knows the truth.

32
00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.120
Because I'm the protagonist.

33
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.000
I lived it.

34
00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.160
Now everyone can tell their story,

35
00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:31.880
and I'll tell mine.

36
00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:49.400
LISBON

37
00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.520
[music playing quietly through radio]

38
00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:04.040
[anchor, in Catalan]
Portuguese footballer Luís Figo

39
00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.680
will be playing the next two seasons
for Barcelona,

40
00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.280
according to sources
in the Portuguese press.

41
00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.200
Figo, 22, a player for Sporting Lisbon,

42
00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:15.480
is currently one of Portugal's
biggest football stars.

43
00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:18.920
Figo will leave this modest neighborhood,

44
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.640
11 kilometers from Lisbon,

45
00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.800
for a life of luxury in Barcelona.

46
00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.240
[Figo, in Spanish] I felt this huge sense
of happiness and joy.

47
00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.960
Barcelona was a team
I followed and admired.

48
00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.800
[indistinct dialogue]

49
00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.880
I felt like a kid with a new ball.

50
00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:43.920
[interviewer speaking in Spanish]

51
00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.080
It was the first trip I made
to play overseas.

52
00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.160
And it was going to be
a completely different reality for me.

53
00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:56.000
A new country, a new championship.
I was very young.

54
00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:01.560
I was going to live on my own.
Not with my parents anymore.

55
00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:16.640
[anchor, in Portuguese] Luís Figo,
until now a Sporting Lisbon player,

56
00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:20.720
arrived in style,
alongside his agent, José Veiga.

57
00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.080
[reporter] Figo! Figo!

58
00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.880
-[reporter 2] Figo! Figo! Figo! Hello.
-[Figo] Hello.

59
00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.880
[reporter, in Spanish]
Are you surprised by this reception?

60
00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:45.320
In a way, but when you consider
the size of the club,

61
00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.520
I'm not that surprised.

62
00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.600
[reporter] Do you realize
you're Barça's star-signing this season

63
00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.200
and that there are
huge expectations for you?

64
00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.000
Sure. I just hope
I can live up to those expectations.

65
00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:03.200
-[reporter] Are you happy, Luís?
-Yes. I'm very happy right now.

66
00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:06.720
["Cant del Barça" plays]

67
00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.760
[Figo] I thought it was a massive club,
where I could get what I wanted,

68
00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:15.120
to gain more prestige and win titles.

69
00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:21.280
And since I was passionate
about Cruyff and his Dream Team,

70
00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.200
I didn't hesitate.

71
00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:37.280
I had the support
of most of the Spanish players.

72
00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:43.320
Especially Pep.

73
00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:50.040
And that helped me fit in
and identify quickly with the club

74
00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.280
and with the culture.

75
00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.600
-Has it been 20 years?
-[interviewer] Yes.

76
00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:00.120
Fuck.

77
00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:06.600
You know what? Maybe I've actually
forgotten a lot of the questions

78
00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.200
I wanted to ask him back then.

79
00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.120
It's crazy how time moves on.

80
00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.720
We were together a lot.

81
00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:22.080
We shared hotel rooms on away games.
We were roommates.

82
00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.480
So we ended up spending
a lot of time together.

83
00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.520
We were inseparable.

84
00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.560
[crowd roaring]

85
00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:40.680
[commentator, in Catalan] Hi from the Nou
Camp, where Barcelona take on Real Madrid.

86
00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:43.160
And here comes the team from the capital.

87
00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.440
[Guardiola] I remember
in Figo's early days,

88
00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:52.280
I went over to Cruyff and said,
"Who the fuck have you signed?"

89
00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:54.400
As in, this guy is very, very good.

90
00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.360
[commentator, in Spanish]
Guardiola to Figo.

91
00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.840
[commentator speaking enthusiastically]

92
00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:12.120
[commentator shouting excitedly]

93
00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:20.520
[Guardiola] During our time together
at Barcelona, he was an amazing player,

94
00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:22.880
in capital letters.

95
00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.400
[commentator 1, in Catalan] Hello
from Santiago Bernabéu Stadium in Madrid.

96
00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:31.080
What an atmosphere
for the Spanish Cup final.

97
00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:36.720
[commentator 2, in Spanish] Barcelona and
Real Betis are just moments from kickoff.

98
00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:42.960
[commentator speaking in Catalan]

99
00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:53.440
The best thing about Luís
was that when you were in trouble,

100
00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:54.440
he'd step up.

101
00:07:59.360 --> 00:08:02.760
[commentator speaking in Catalan]

102
00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:09.120
1-1
FIGO, MINUTE 45

103
00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.880
[commentator shouting enthusiastically]

104
00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:17.480
[Guardiola] There are many great players
who, when the going gets tough,

105
00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.760
struggle sometimes.

106
00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:23.760
He was the complete opposite.

107
00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.640
If things were tough,
he'd say, "Give me the ball,"

108
00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:31.040
and he'd try to find a way
to change things.

109
00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:36.920
[commentator speaking in Catalan]

110
00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:45.120
[commentator speaking excitedly]

111
00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.720
[commentator 2, in English]
Barcelona have scored

112
00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:49.480
what I think might be the winner!

113
00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:54.080
FIGO
GOALS 2

114
00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:56.160
[commentator speaking in Catalan]

115
00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:01.920
[in Catalan] Here it is!

116
00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:09.200
[in Spanish]
Who scored the winning goal yesterday?

117
00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:10.880
[crowd] Figo!

118
00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:15.120
[chanting in Spanish]
Don't stop, Figo, Figo!

119
00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:18.480
Don't stop, Figo, Figo!

120
00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:21.120
Don't stop, Figo, Figo! Don't stop…

121
00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:24.560
[reporter, in Portuguese]
You can get a Figo calendar, a postcard,

122
00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.600
a poster,

123
00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:30.520
and Figo's number-seven shirt.

124
00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:32.960
It's truly Figo-mania.

125
00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.960
[commentator 1, in English]
Welcome to the Nou Camp.

126
00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:39.600
And there's no bigger game than this.

127
00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.600
It's Barcelona against Real Madrid.

128
00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:44.000
El Clásico.

129
00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:47.320
[commentator 2, in Spanish]
Here at the Nou Camp,

130
00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:52.040
Barcelona can become

131
00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:57.920
the 1997-98 league champions.

132
00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:04.720
Playing against Luís Figo is to suffer.

133
00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:12.280
Playing against Luís
meant not sleeping well at night.

134
00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:15.240
He was the captain of Barcelona,
and my job was to mark him.

135
00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.960
I knew what I had to do,
but it was impossible.

136
00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:22.080
[commentator speaking in Spanish]

137
00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:31.880
[Carlos] He was number one in the world.

138
00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:35.000
[commentator speaking in Catalan]

139
00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:38.720
[commentator 3, in Spanish]
Barcelona can taste

140
00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:41.200
the sweet victory of a league title.

141
00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:42.520
[commentary continues]

142
00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.080
[Carlos] To say that Figo
was the symbol of the club

143
00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:56.400
sums up perfectly his time at Barcelona.

144
00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:03.040
[Figo] I identified
with the values of the club.

145
00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:04.800
I defended them to the death.

146
00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:11.080
And that's why I think
I was seen as one of them.

147
00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:16.560
[in Spanish] I think there are certain
people that should congratulate us.

148
00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:19.200
[spectators cheering raucously]

149
00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.680
[chanting] Madrid crybabies!
Bow down to the champions!

150
00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:25.880
Madrid crybabies!
Bow down to the champions!

151
00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:27.360
Long live Barça!

152
00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:32.280
[commentator speaking in Spanish]

153
00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:37.080
[commentator shouts joyfully]

154
00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:48.920
[commentator] Barcelona
are the 1998-99 league champions!

155
00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:54.080
This is their sixth league title
of the '90s.

156
00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:56.320
They've won as many titles
this decade alone

157
00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.960
as they have in the past 40 years.

158
00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.920
[reporter, in Spanish]
Luís, first of all, congratulations.

159
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.120
Is this concrete evidence
of Barcelona's current superiority?

160
00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:12.240
[in Spanish] Well, right now,
I think Barça has amazing professionals,

161
00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:16.720
amazing, uh, uh, players,

162
00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:19.200
and we're definitely
the best club in the world.

163
00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.440
Champions, man!

164
00:12:21.520 --> 00:12:22.640
We're the best.

165
00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.080
Long live Barça!

166
00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:27.160
[man speaking in Spanish]

167
00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:31.000
[Figo, present] We won the league
two seasons in a row.

168
00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:34.800
We won because we were the best.

169
00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.040
-[Figo singing]
-[people clapping]

170
00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:50.840
[Figo, present] It was a fantastic period
for me, and at such a young age.

171
00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:53.440
It was also when I met my wife.

172
00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.800
My first daughter was born in Barcelona.

173
00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.360
The truth is, I was very happy.

174
00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:08.560
[Figo, in Portuguese] It's 31st March.

175
00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:12.880
Daniela just turned one,

176
00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:16.200
and we're celebrating at home.

177
00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:19.280
[people singing
"Happy Birthday" in Spanish]

178
00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:43.120
[interviewer] Do you remember
Figo's last season?

179
00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.480
Did he seem unhappy?

180
00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:46.680
Did he mention anything
about his contract?

181
00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:47.600
No.

182
00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:49.520
No, never.

183
00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:52.600
He had a great knack
of separating football

184
00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:55.600
from life off the pitch. Uh…

185
00:13:57.240 --> 00:14:00.800
I remember in his final months,
there were so many rumors about that.

186
00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:05.480
We talked about it. About how he was.

187
00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:09.000
He said he was fine
and what would be would be.

188
00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.480
But he was his usual self.

189
00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:21.280
[Figo, present] I was happy
in the city and at the club.

190
00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:27.680
But what was important for me

191
00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.600
was to feel valued
for what I gave to the club.

192
00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:40.720
Perhaps there were times
when I didn't feel as valued

193
00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:42.360
by those in charge at the club

194
00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:48.440
compared to the team supporters, the fans.

195
00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.480
For me, happiness was playing football

196
00:14:56.560 --> 00:14:58.000
and the recognition I got.

197
00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:04.560
[commentator speaking Spanish]

198
00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:16.000
[in Spanish] I can't comment.
I don't know what will happen.

199
00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:20.120
But I hope things get resolved,

200
00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:21.760
and we can all relax.

201
00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:25.760
I was going to say, "Enjoy your time off,"
but you don't get time off.

202
00:15:25.840 --> 00:15:28.120
-So, good luck at the Euros.
-Thank you.

203
00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:32.000
When you feel that way,

204
00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.480
so people don't appreciate what you give,

205
00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:42.040
then maybe there's another club
that will acknowledge you.

206
00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:45.680
["Zadok the Priest"
by Handel plays through TV]

207
00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:48.840
[commentator, in English]
Despite yet another

208
00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:53.000
disappointing season domestically,
but Real Madrid are one game away

209
00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:55.520
from conquering Europe once again.

210
00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:00.160
Madrid face Valencia
in an all-Spanish Champions League final.

211
00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:03.760
[commentator speaking in Spanish]

212
00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:09.320
[commentator speaking
with growing excitement]

213
00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:16.560
[commentator yelling enthusiastically]

214
00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:25.360
[commentator, shouting]
Real Madrid, three-nil!

215
00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:30.480
Real Madrid can now count
up to eight European Cups!

216
00:16:33.040 --> 00:16:36.520
The culture at Real Madrid means that
you have to play in the Champions League

217
00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:37.440
and win it.

218
00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.760
[chanting indistinctly]

219
00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:42.680
[Carlos] Our preparation
was always focused on the European Cup

220
00:16:42.760 --> 00:16:45.240
because of how long it had been
since we'd won it.

221
00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:53.240
For me,

222
00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:57.320
there's no doubt it's the key moment
in Real Madrid's recent history.

223
00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:58.440
No doubt at all.

224
00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:00.960
[celebratory music plays]

225
00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:06.040
[Hierro] It restored
the club's power and status in Europe.

226
00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.080
[chanting]

227
00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:15.320
[Hierro] Those two Champions Leagues
won under Lorenzo Sanz

228
00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:16.640
were great for the club.

229
00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:20.400
["Hala Madrid!"
by José de Aguilar playing]

230
00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:27.840
[Hierro] As a president,
Lorenzo was extremely warmhearted.

231
00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:30.720
He was very close to us,
like a father figure.

232
00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:33.800
["Hala Madrid!" continues]

233
00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:47.760
Spain is a unique country
where the presidents are the stars.

234
00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:50.640
They have a strong public presence.

235
00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:54.520
They have a strong presence
within the team and in the dressing room.

236
00:17:56.480 --> 00:17:59.840
The president needs to be
front and center as a symbol for the club.

237
00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:08.040
[in Spanish] It's official.
This summer, Real Madrid's members

238
00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:09.800
will have to vote for their president.

239
00:18:09.880 --> 00:18:12.360
Lorenzo Sanz
has one year left as president

240
00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:15.640
but has decided
that this is the right time

241
00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:17.560
to ensure another term in charge.

242
00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.160
[anchor 1, in Spanish] Now we wait and see

243
00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.280
if there's a candidate
capable of challenging

244
00:18:22.360 --> 00:18:26.480
a president who's won
two Champions Leagues in three years.

245
00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:33.720
[anchor 2, in Spanish] Today, we have
a very special guest on our program.

246
00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:38.520
He's 53 years old.
He's a civil engineer. He's married.

247
00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:42.160
He's been a member
of Real Madrid for 40 years.

248
00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.920
[unheard dialogue]

249
00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:49.720
[anchor 3, in Spanish]
Please welcome Florentino Pérez.

250
00:18:49.800 --> 00:18:51.160
[Pérez, in Spanish] Good evening.

251
00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:56.120
[anchor 2, in Spanish]
Are you Real Madrid's next president?

252
00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:57.400
I am sure of it.

253
00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:04.920
We knew he was an important
and powerful businessman

254
00:19:05.000 --> 00:19:06.120
who loved football.

255
00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:10.800
And he had put himself forward as a
candidate in the presidential elections.

256
00:19:12.320 --> 00:19:14.520
THIS IS HOW MADRID WINS

257
00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:16.480
But we didn't know much about him.

258
00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:25.200
[interviewer] Why do you think someone
want to be president of a football club?

259
00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:29.040
For many reasons.

260
00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:31.640
Why would someone
want to be president of a nation?

261
00:19:32.160 --> 00:19:34.560
For the power. To call the shots.

262
00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:38.720
In Florentino's case, he'd been at Madrid
since the day he was born.

263
00:19:38.800 --> 00:19:40.280
His father made him a member.

264
00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:44.440
And I think that it's his life.
It's been his whole life.

265
00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:51.440
To me, as a man,

266
00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:54.200
he was just as calculating then
as he is now.

267
00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:56.960
Just as emotionally cold,

268
00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:59.960
but perhaps he was more naive
about the world of football

269
00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:00.880
than he is now.

270
00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:06.600
REAL MADRID PRESIDENTIAL CAMPAIGN
FLORENTINO PÉREZ

271
00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:10.040
Football's about results.

272
00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.920
Real Madrid had just won
two Champions Leagues,

273
00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:14.680
and I thought,
"How's Florentino gonna win?"

274
00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:18.520
He put out this message
that even though Real Madrid

275
00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:21.160
had won two Champions Leagues,
pretty much back-to-back,

276
00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:23.960
something was missing.

277
00:20:24.040 --> 00:20:27.320
They needed players of a certain caliber
to restore a reputation,

278
00:20:27.400 --> 00:20:30.280
which in his view,
had faded on the international stage.

279
00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:32.360
[unheard dialogue]

280
00:20:35.000 --> 00:20:37.560
[Pérez, in Spanish] There are two ways
of winning. In small letters

281
00:20:37.640 --> 00:20:38.840
or in capital letters,

282
00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:43.120
which is the way the teams of Real Madrid
have always won in the past.

283
00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:47.200
What I want to do
is win in capital letters.

284
00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:52.520
That's why this is the best-known
and most prestigious club in the world.

285
00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:54.880
This club, as everyone knows,

286
00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:57.240
has been declared
Club of the Century by FIFA,

287
00:20:57.320 --> 00:21:03.080
and this is because of its unique style
and way of acting.

288
00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:06.560
Unfortunately,
we're far from that image now.

289
00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:12.600
[TV commentator, in Spanish] There was
nothing that could stop Di Stéfano.

290
00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:18.680
Real Madrid has won
the very first European Cup.

291
00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:32.320
Madrid is unique,
firstly, because of its history.

292
00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:35.320
[commentator, in Spanish]
This amazing feat by Real Madrid

293
00:21:35.400 --> 00:21:38.960
justifies the huge show of support
by their fans.

294
00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:41.080
[commentator speaking in Spanish]

295
00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:45.600
[commentators shouting with delight]

296
00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:56.760
Precisely because they don't have

297
00:21:56.840 --> 00:22:00.360
a clear cultural, social,
or political identity as such,

298
00:22:01.240 --> 00:22:03.840
Real Madrid's imperative is to win.

299
00:22:04.600 --> 00:22:06.600
[commentator speaking in Spanish]

300
00:22:21.400 --> 00:22:24.680
[Valdano] Florentino Pérez
had a mythical ideology of Real Madrid.

301
00:22:26.960 --> 00:22:29.800
He'd always idealized the club,

302
00:22:30.320 --> 00:22:32.920
and he wanted to make the club
live up to this ideal.

303
00:22:34.760 --> 00:22:38.600
[interviewer, in Spanish] Mr. Pérez,
best of luck in your election campaign.

304
00:22:38.680 --> 00:22:41.040
Thank you so much
for giving me the opportunity

305
00:22:41.120 --> 00:22:43.360
to talk to you and my fellow members.

306
00:22:43.440 --> 00:22:45.440
[indistinct dialogue]

307
00:22:47.640 --> 00:22:50.120
[De la Morena] I remember
having lunch with him and telling him

308
00:22:50.200 --> 00:22:52.200
I thought it was practically impossible.

309
00:22:53.800 --> 00:22:55.480
I said, "You have a glass jaw,

310
00:22:56.640 --> 00:22:58.360
and in the world of football,

311
00:22:58.440 --> 00:23:01.200
where everyone has a loaded tommy gun
under their coats,

312
00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:02.680
you won't last two days."

313
00:23:02.760 --> 00:23:05.360
And he said, "Well, that's what you think.
In the business world--"

314
00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:08.320
I said, "The business world
has nothing to do with this."

315
00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:09.680
"This is very different."

316
00:23:15.880 --> 00:23:19.360
[interviewer] When did Florentino
first mention the plan to sign Figo?

317
00:23:21.720 --> 00:23:24.240
At our first meeting.
He asked for my thoughts on the player.

318
00:23:25.200 --> 00:23:27.680
He sees football as a heroes' business,

319
00:23:29.320 --> 00:23:32.480
and he set his sights
on the best in the world from day one.

320
00:23:34.880 --> 00:23:38.760
4 WEEKS TO THE ELECTIONS

321
00:23:40.720 --> 00:23:42.200
[cellphone rings]

322
00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:44.680
[man] I was at home.
A friend of mine called me.

323
00:23:46.760 --> 00:23:48.520
He said, "Hey, man. Where are you?"

324
00:23:48.600 --> 00:23:51.400
I said, "I'm in Madrid."
He replied, "Come here now."

325
00:23:51.480 --> 00:23:53.320
"It's urgent. Can you come here now?"

326
00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:55.840
[stopwatch ticking]

327
00:23:57.240 --> 00:23:59.200
[Futre] I saw this impressive building.

328
00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:02.280
I went inside.

329
00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:06.520
The secretary took me to an office

330
00:24:06.600 --> 00:24:08.760
and introduced me to Florentino Pérez.

331
00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:13.880
It was the first time
that I'd ever heard that name.

332
00:24:18.600 --> 00:24:22.000
This man is running
in the Real Madrid presidential elections.

333
00:24:25.160 --> 00:24:28.520
But he'll only run
if Luís Figo joins with him.

334
00:24:29.880 --> 00:24:32.560
I thought it had to be a joke.
What was I doing there?

335
00:24:34.920 --> 00:24:37.040
[interviewer]
How would you describe Paulo?

336
00:24:37.120 --> 00:24:38.160
Spectacular.

337
00:24:38.880 --> 00:24:40.040
He's spectacular.

338
00:24:40.840 --> 00:24:41.960
Paulo was my hero.

339
00:24:44.880 --> 00:24:47.520
-[commentator, in Spanish] It's Futre!
-[crowd roars]

340
00:24:49.680 --> 00:24:53.560
[Figo, present] He was Portugal's
best player, so I grew up admiring Paulo.

341
00:24:58.400 --> 00:25:00.200
And then, and I don't know how,

342
00:25:00.280 --> 00:25:02.240
he became involved in my transfer.

343
00:25:03.640 --> 00:25:05.400
Paulo's capable of anything.

344
00:25:05.480 --> 00:25:07.480
[tense rhythmic music plays]

345
00:25:10.440 --> 00:25:12.960
[Futre] Figo had
a €60 million release clause.

346
00:25:15.640 --> 00:25:16.720
Who's paying that?!

347
00:25:20.480 --> 00:25:21.720
"Don't worry," he said.

348
00:25:21.800 --> 00:25:23.320
[in Portuguese] "I'll pay it."

349
00:25:24.520 --> 00:25:26.080
[cellphone rings]

350
00:25:26.960 --> 00:25:30.960
[Futre] So then I called Figo's agent,
José Veiga, who was a good friend of mine.

351
00:25:31.920 --> 00:25:33.880
[cellphone rings]

352
00:25:40.200 --> 00:25:42.720
Back then,
I was the top agent in football.

353
00:25:44.920 --> 00:25:47.080
[in Portuguese]
"Hey, José. How's it going?"

354
00:25:49.560 --> 00:25:52.800
And I was like,
"Paulo, please. Don't call me."

355
00:25:52.880 --> 00:25:55.120
He called me in the evening
to tell me there's a candidate

356
00:25:55.200 --> 00:25:58.320
trying to win Real Madrid's elections
who wants to sign Figo.

357
00:25:58.800 --> 00:26:01.040
"It's not possible. No, Paulo. Let it go."

358
00:26:01.120 --> 00:26:03.320
"Let's talk another time, not now."

359
00:26:03.400 --> 00:26:04.960
Then he hung up on me.

360
00:26:10.880 --> 00:26:14.120
But I kept the phone to my ear.
And I keep on talking.

361
00:26:14.200 --> 00:26:16.200
And I was like, "Yes, sir. Okay."

362
00:26:17.240 --> 00:26:19.240
[tense music continues]

363
00:26:20.200 --> 00:26:24.720
[Futre] And those 30 to 40 seconds,
when I was pretending to talk to José,

364
00:26:26.960 --> 00:26:29.080
are key to the whole operation.

365
00:26:34.280 --> 00:26:35.640
So what was I thinking?

366
00:26:35.720 --> 00:26:39.920
If Florentino Pérez
can pay €72 million in cash,

367
00:26:42.920 --> 00:26:44.160
he can afford more.

368
00:26:44.240 --> 00:26:45.840
Cogs were turning in my head.

369
00:26:47.200 --> 00:26:49.000
So I put the phone on the table,

370
00:26:49.920 --> 00:26:51.240
and I say to Florentino,

371
00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:53.480
"He wants €10 million in commission."

372
00:26:54.280 --> 00:26:55.440
And he says,

373
00:26:55.520 --> 00:26:56.480
"€5 million."

374
00:26:56.560 --> 00:26:57.960
And we shook on six.

375
00:27:00.520 --> 00:27:02.040
[phone ringing]

376
00:27:02.520 --> 00:27:05.240
[Veiga] Paulo never stops,
and he called me again.

377
00:27:07.560 --> 00:27:10.120
"Man, this is
a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity."

378
00:27:10.200 --> 00:27:11.440
"It's unprecedented."

379
00:27:11.520 --> 00:27:13.400
It was classic Paulo Futre.

380
00:27:14.400 --> 00:27:18.040
"Zé, calm down. Don't hang up.
Calm down. Six million in commission."

381
00:27:19.240 --> 00:27:22.520
[in Portuguese] "€6 million
in commission waiting for us."

382
00:27:23.240 --> 00:27:25.120
"Calm down. Don't hang up!"

383
00:27:25.720 --> 00:27:27.960
And then José said, "What?!"

384
00:27:28.040 --> 00:27:29.920
"€6 million in commission?"

385
00:27:33.400 --> 00:27:35.600
And that day, the Luís Figo saga began.

386
00:27:35.680 --> 00:27:37.520
It's incredible it began with a lie.

387
00:27:43.560 --> 00:27:46.080
[Veiga] So I went to meet
with Florentino Pérez

388
00:27:46.160 --> 00:27:48.320
in his office at ACS in Madrid.

389
00:27:51.120 --> 00:27:53.640
Don Florentino
explained the project to me.

390
00:27:56.360 --> 00:27:59.960
Everything he said made sense,
but it would be very difficult to execute.

391
00:28:03.240 --> 00:28:06.320
So I said, "I'll have a word with Luís
and get back to you."

392
00:28:09.320 --> 00:28:12.840
Luís Figo was in the Netherlands
for the European Championships,

393
00:28:13.360 --> 00:28:14.720
so I headed straight there.

394
00:28:19.080 --> 00:28:22.560
PORTUGAL TRAINING CAMP
EURO 2000

395
00:28:23.920 --> 00:28:29.160
[reporter, in Portuguese] This morning,
José Veiga arrived at Portugal's hotel.

396
00:28:29.240 --> 00:28:31.520
José Veiga is Luís Figo's agent.

397
00:28:31.600 --> 00:28:35.640
Veiga is likely to be discussing
the player's future.

398
00:28:38.640 --> 00:28:41.480
[Figo] The information I had
was that there's this person

399
00:28:42.000 --> 00:28:43.280
who I didn't know at all.

400
00:28:44.160 --> 00:28:46.440
"There's this person
who wants you to sign for Madrid."

401
00:28:46.520 --> 00:28:48.120
"If he wins the elections."

402
00:28:50.600 --> 00:28:53.680
"He wants you to say
that you'll sign for Madrid if he wins."

403
00:28:54.240 --> 00:28:55.440
I said, "Are you crazy?"

404
00:28:55.960 --> 00:28:58.880
"How can I say to someone,
when I don't even know if he's gonna win,

405
00:28:58.960 --> 00:29:02.400
that I'll go to Real Madrid,
when I have a contract at Barcelona?"

406
00:29:02.480 --> 00:29:04.600
"There's no way I can do that. Ever."

407
00:29:08.560 --> 00:29:10.880
No club had ever spent
so much on a player.

408
00:29:13.000 --> 00:29:16.120
They were offering four times
what I was making at Barcelona.

409
00:29:20.160 --> 00:29:22.440
It was something
that I found hard to believe.

410
00:29:23.800 --> 00:29:26.640
-[fans, chanting] Figo!
-[Figo] It was a strange summer

411
00:29:26.720 --> 00:29:29.800
because there were also
presidential elections at Barcelona.

412
00:29:32.160 --> 00:29:35.280
It's unusual for both clubs
to have elections at the same time.

413
00:29:35.360 --> 00:29:36.640
But that's what happened.

414
00:29:39.880 --> 00:29:41.680
I said to my agent, "Keep talking."

415
00:29:42.200 --> 00:29:46.280
"Keep talking with the relevant people.
Keep talking, and let's see what happens."

416
00:29:47.640 --> 00:29:50.040
Luís said, "Okay, go to Barcelona,

417
00:29:50.120 --> 00:29:53.320
and see if there's a possibility
that my contract can be improved."

418
00:29:53.400 --> 00:29:55.560
"If they do that, I'll stay at Barça."

419
00:29:56.920 --> 00:29:58.520
[crowd cheering]

420
00:29:58.600 --> 00:30:01.240
["Cant del Barça" plays]

421
00:30:01.320 --> 00:30:03.720
[anchor, in Spanish] The race for
Barça's next president has begun.

422
00:30:03.800 --> 00:30:09.120
Joan Gaspart is the big favorite
to succeed the current president.

423
00:30:10.280 --> 00:30:14.240
[in Catalan] It's the end
of an era at Barcelona

424
00:30:14.320 --> 00:30:17.920
but the beginning of a new one.

425
00:30:18.440 --> 00:30:24.400
And Barça's members
can choose a new president.

426
00:30:24.480 --> 00:30:25.680
PASSION FOR BARÇA

427
00:30:26.440 --> 00:30:28.440
[Gaspart] My candidacy was very easy.

428
00:30:29.480 --> 00:30:33.000
I didn't have to present myself
to the members of Barça and tell them,

429
00:30:33.080 --> 00:30:34.040
"Vote for me."

430
00:30:34.640 --> 00:30:38.320
All I said was, "Here I am.
I've been vice president for 22 years."

431
00:30:38.400 --> 00:30:40.640
"You already know
the good and bad about me."

432
00:30:41.560 --> 00:30:44.560
[in Catalan] Get it into your head.
Barça is the best club in the world.

433
00:30:44.640 --> 00:30:48.280
Don't say that we need to make Barça
the best club in the world. It already is!

434
00:30:55.600 --> 00:30:59.040
[Veiga] The Joan Gaspart I know
isn't an easy character to deal with.

435
00:30:59.120 --> 00:31:02.720
He was viewed as a person
who loved his dear Barcelona,

436
00:31:02.800 --> 00:31:04.120
which is indisputable,

437
00:31:06.280 --> 00:31:09.200
but he was also someone
who made promises he didn't keep.

438
00:31:13.840 --> 00:31:18.120
So, when it came to trusting his word,
he always left you with doubts.

439
00:31:19.320 --> 00:31:21.320
[speaking Catalan]

440
00:31:24.720 --> 00:31:26.160
[Veiga] I went to Barcelona,

441
00:31:27.960 --> 00:31:29.720
and I said to Joan Gaspart

442
00:31:29.800 --> 00:31:31.920
that we have an offer
that we can't refuse.

443
00:31:32.440 --> 00:31:34.200
I didn't mention the club involved.

444
00:31:35.720 --> 00:31:37.400
But I said, "We would like to see

445
00:31:37.480 --> 00:31:41.280
if we could improve the terms
and conditions of Luís Figo's contract."

446
00:31:44.120 --> 00:31:46.680
It was a kind of obsession that Luís had.

447
00:31:47.560 --> 00:31:50.520
From time to time,
he or Veiga would ask for more money.

448
00:31:51.960 --> 00:31:54.080
But that's normal
in the world of football.

449
00:31:56.960 --> 00:31:59.480
[Veiga] And Joan Gaspart replied,
"No, that's unthinkable."

450
00:31:59.560 --> 00:32:01.440
"No way. I'm not going to do it."

451
00:32:01.520 --> 00:32:03.880
"I'm not renewing
anybody's contract right now."

452
00:32:03.960 --> 00:32:06.040
"Anyway, there are going to be elections,

453
00:32:06.120 --> 00:32:09.160
and during this process,
we're not renewing any contracts."

454
00:32:11.200 --> 00:32:14.880
[in Spanish] Figo has a contract with
Barça, which ends in three or four years.

455
00:32:14.960 --> 00:32:16.720
He wants to improve his contract,

456
00:32:16.800 --> 00:32:20.800
but right now,
we have no intention of doing so,

457
00:32:20.880 --> 00:32:22.440
because we did that a year ago.

458
00:32:24.880 --> 00:32:27.600
[commentator, in English]
So much attention on Figo

459
00:32:27.680 --> 00:32:30.960
as Portugal begin
their Euro 2000 campaign.

460
00:32:32.440 --> 00:32:33.400
[commentator] Figo.

461
00:32:35.800 --> 00:32:37.400
[spectators cheer raucously]

462
00:32:37.480 --> 00:32:39.400
[commentator, in English] Oh, goodness me!

463
00:32:42.680 --> 00:32:46.120
[Figo, in Spanish] The president says
he can't solve anything,

464
00:32:46.200 --> 00:32:49.200
and I should talk to the candidates.

465
00:32:49.280 --> 00:32:52.880
The candidates say
they don't have the power to negotiate,

466
00:32:52.960 --> 00:32:55.080
and I should talk to the president.

467
00:32:55.160 --> 00:33:00.640
So I'm being sent from one to the other.

468
00:33:02.920 --> 00:33:05.840
People talk about feelings,
which, of course, I have,

469
00:33:05.920 --> 00:33:08.160
but I need those feelings
to be reciprocated.

470
00:33:08.680 --> 00:33:10.800
At the end of the day,
it's a relationship.

471
00:33:12.080 --> 00:33:17.000
[in Spanish] But it seems like
no one is willing to listen to me

472
00:33:17.080 --> 00:33:18.560
in order to make a decision.

473
00:33:19.200 --> 00:33:20.680
I went back to the Netherlands.

474
00:33:26.760 --> 00:33:30.440
I explained the situation to Luís Figo,
and he said to me,

475
00:33:30.520 --> 00:33:32.160
"I'd like to stay at Barcelona."

476
00:33:35.720 --> 00:33:38.080
[English commentator 1]
It's Portugal and Turkey

477
00:33:38.160 --> 00:33:40.480
for a place in the semifinals.

478
00:33:41.480 --> 00:33:42.880
[English commentator 2] Simply done.

479
00:33:42.960 --> 00:33:45.480
Ünsal trying to make something of it.
Referee doesn't wanna know!

480
00:33:45.560 --> 00:33:46.560
And that's a second.

481
00:33:50.200 --> 00:33:52.760
"Go and speak to Joan Gaspart
one last time."

482
00:33:56.360 --> 00:33:58.240
"Joan, let's be really clear."

483
00:33:58.720 --> 00:33:59.720
"This is serious."

484
00:34:03.480 --> 00:34:06.760
"If we don't reach an agreement
and you don't make a move,

485
00:34:06.840 --> 00:34:08.920
Barcelona will lose Luís Figo."

486
00:34:10.160 --> 00:34:11.680
"No! That's impossible."

487
00:34:11.760 --> 00:34:14.880
"You're trying to negotiate with me.
You're blackmailing me."

488
00:34:15.600 --> 00:34:18.920
"If someone pays the release clause,
if someone brings the check,

489
00:34:20.200 --> 00:34:22.040
then I'll pay for you and Luís Figo

490
00:34:22.120 --> 00:34:25.480
to fly first-class
on a red velvet carpet out of here."

491
00:34:27.320 --> 00:34:29.800
"Bring the check for the release clause
because I don't believe

492
00:34:29.880 --> 00:34:32.480
there's a club in the world
that can pay that amount."

493
00:34:36.000 --> 00:34:38.800
So I said,
"Okay, Joan, if that's what you want,

494
00:34:38.880 --> 00:34:41.280
that's fine,
then we're going to move forward."

495
00:34:42.960 --> 00:34:44.440
So I called Luís Figo.

496
00:34:44.520 --> 00:34:46.280
[answering machine clicks, beeps]

497
00:34:46.360 --> 00:34:49.800
[Veiga, in Portuguese] There's clearly
a lack of will here so far.

498
00:34:50.840 --> 00:34:55.480
Look, when people want to solve problems,
they will solve them.

499
00:34:57.760 --> 00:34:59.840
[Figo] Gaspart treated me like a nobody.

500
00:35:02.160 --> 00:35:06.480
It wasn't something I was expecting.
I'd expected maybe a bit more warmth.

501
00:35:06.560 --> 00:35:07.840
Some kind of recognition.

502
00:35:10.880 --> 00:35:12.560
And I felt a bit pissed off.

503
00:35:13.640 --> 00:35:15.640
I went away
after speaking with him, thinking,

504
00:35:15.720 --> 00:35:18.280
"For fuck's sake,
this guy thinks it's all a bluff."

505
00:35:19.400 --> 00:35:21.440
"A way to improve my contract again."

506
00:35:23.760 --> 00:35:26.120
So it all started
because I was pissed off.

507
00:35:29.520 --> 00:35:32.960
[commentator, in English]
The Euro 2000 semifinal in Brussels.

508
00:35:33.040 --> 00:35:34.960
France against Portugal.

509
00:35:39.120 --> 00:35:40.240
And Zidane scores!

510
00:35:40.320 --> 00:35:42.600
And France are in the final!

511
00:35:43.720 --> 00:35:47.640
Luís Figo and his Portuguese team
are heading home.

512
00:35:47.720 --> 00:35:51.320
[in Portuguese] You're here with Portugal,
but talking of personal matters,

513
00:35:51.400 --> 00:35:53.200
will you stay with Barcelona next season?

514
00:35:53.280 --> 00:35:55.400
[in Portuguese]
Let's not speak about me. Just Portugal.

515
00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:57.280
When will you speak about yourself?

516
00:35:57.360 --> 00:35:58.960
I never speak about myself.

517
00:35:59.040 --> 00:36:03.720
So you won't comment
on which club you'll be playing for?

518
00:36:03.800 --> 00:36:06.960
Look, I have a contract,
and I expect to fulfill it.

519
00:36:07.640 --> 00:36:08.680
[paparazzo] Figo!

520
00:36:09.480 --> 00:36:10.760
[Figo] I went on holiday.

521
00:36:13.280 --> 00:36:17.000
And a few weeks later,
I think things really began to develop,

522
00:36:18.680 --> 00:36:20.160
and they started to snowball.

523
00:36:24.480 --> 00:36:26.400
And then it became a lot more serious.

524
00:36:33.480 --> 00:36:35.720
11 DAYS TO THE ELECTIONS

525
00:36:35.800 --> 00:36:38.160
[De la Morena]
Someone leaked a story to me one night.

526
00:36:38.840 --> 00:36:41.320
That Florentino
might be trying to sign Figo.

527
00:36:43.160 --> 00:36:44.440
I spoke with Florentino.

528
00:36:45.360 --> 00:36:48.200
He got quite flustered
and said it wasn't true.

529
00:36:48.280 --> 00:36:51.040
Then he said it was true.
And I said, "I'm running the story."

530
00:36:51.120 --> 00:36:53.800
Then he said, "If you run it,
you'll fuck things up for me."

531
00:36:53.880 --> 00:36:56.320
"Don't do it.
Shit. You'll fuck everything up for me."

532
00:36:56.400 --> 00:36:58.480
And I said, "I'm running it at midnight."

533
00:37:01.880 --> 00:37:04.440
["Ra, Ra, Ra" by Benito Moreno plays]

534
00:37:14.520 --> 00:37:17.320
[De la Morena] It was a Wednesday.
Míchel Salgado was getting married

535
00:37:17.400 --> 00:37:18.840
to Lorenzo Sanz's daughter.

536
00:37:18.920 --> 00:37:20.040
I was at the wedding.

537
00:37:20.720 --> 00:37:23.360
[reporter, in Spanish] You more nervous
for the wedding or elections?

538
00:37:23.440 --> 00:37:25.280
[in Spanish] I'm not thinking
about the elections today.

539
00:37:28.480 --> 00:37:31.440
[De la Morena] How could I know
that MARCA wouldn't leak the story online?

540
00:37:31.520 --> 00:37:34.120
They could leak it first.
"Figo signs for Madrid."

541
00:37:34.200 --> 00:37:35.760
Then the story's theirs.

542
00:37:36.480 --> 00:37:37.680
So I look at the time.

543
00:37:37.760 --> 00:37:40.680
It was 6:20 p.m.
Right in the middle of the ceremony.

544
00:37:41.920 --> 00:37:44.400
I left the church.
I wasn't waiting till midnight.

545
00:37:44.480 --> 00:37:46.240
I'd break it at 8:30 p.m.

546
00:37:47.680 --> 00:37:49.680
[journalists speaking indistinctly]

547
00:37:50.680 --> 00:37:52.960
-[camera shutters click]
-[speaks Spanish]

548
00:37:53.560 --> 00:37:55.160
I got into my car.

549
00:37:55.240 --> 00:37:57.960
-[electronic beep]
-I heard the beeps. Cadena SER news.

550
00:38:00.080 --> 00:38:01.920
[Cadena SER jingle plays]

551
00:38:03.520 --> 00:38:06.080
[De la Morena, in Spanish]
Figo will be Real Madrid's new signing

552
00:38:06.160 --> 00:38:09.720
if Florentino Pérez becomes president.

553
00:38:11.960 --> 00:38:14.680
Then I came up
with a story to make it even bigger.

554
00:38:14.760 --> 00:38:18.160
I said, "Florentino has said
that if Figo doesn't come to Madrid,

555
00:38:18.240 --> 00:38:21.360
he'll pay every fan's season ticket
and club membership fees."

556
00:38:22.040 --> 00:38:23.320
I made that part up.

557
00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:27.240
Florentino called me,

558
00:38:27.320 --> 00:38:29.480
"You bastard,
do you know what you've done?"

559
00:38:29.560 --> 00:38:31.760
"And you even said
I'll pay the membership fees!"

560
00:38:32.280 --> 00:38:34.240
In the car behind me was Lorenzo Sanz.

561
00:38:34.320 --> 00:38:36.160
And he hears the news in the car.

562
00:38:38.800 --> 00:38:42.480
When we arrived at the reception,
Lorenzo sees me and shouts at me,

563
00:38:45.000 --> 00:38:47.800
"They made a fool out of you!
You've fallen for it."

564
00:38:47.880 --> 00:38:50.880
And I said,
"You tend to the bride. That's your job."

565
00:38:52.200 --> 00:38:53.200
And he kept on and on.

566
00:38:53.280 --> 00:38:57.400
"You've made an idiot of yourself.
They've played you. They've played you."

567
00:38:57.480 --> 00:38:59.880
After that, it was the only news in town.

568
00:39:03.440 --> 00:39:06.760
[in Spanish] Cadena SER
has broken the news that Florentino Pérez,

569
00:39:06.840 --> 00:39:09.360
one of Real Madrid's
presidential candidates,

570
00:39:09.440 --> 00:39:11.400
may have sealed the signing of Luís Figo.

571
00:39:11.480 --> 00:39:16.000
[in Spanish] Everything suggests
Florentino Pérez has signed Luís Figo…

572
00:39:16.080 --> 00:39:19.480
…one of the best players in the world.
But he won't leave for free.

573
00:39:19.560 --> 00:39:21.520
€60 million is his asking price,

574
00:39:21.600 --> 00:39:24.440
making him the most expensive player
of all time.

575
00:39:27.480 --> 00:39:29.440
FIGO IS FLORENTINO'S BOMBSHELL

576
00:39:29.520 --> 00:39:31.400
FIGO IS THE BOMBSHELL

577
00:39:32.480 --> 00:39:33.800
It was a real bombshell.

578
00:39:34.320 --> 00:39:36.800
However, at the time,
all of us were saying, "It's impossible."

579
00:39:36.880 --> 00:39:40.400
Because it was impossible.
Back then, it seemed totally impossible.

580
00:39:42.080 --> 00:39:44.560
It would be like
Real Madrid signing Messi.

581
00:39:46.800 --> 00:39:50.840
[in Spanish] Impossible. Like saying
you want to take Raúl from Real Madrid.

582
00:39:50.920 --> 00:39:54.440
What would the Real Madrid squad say?
What would the other players say?

583
00:39:56.000 --> 00:39:57.920
We were all on holiday
when the rumor started

584
00:39:58.000 --> 00:40:00.080
that Figo was coming here to the club.

585
00:40:00.600 --> 00:40:01.920
I didn't believe it.

586
00:40:04.880 --> 00:40:06.840
I talked to some of the other guys
on the phone,

587
00:40:06.920 --> 00:40:08.400
like Iker and Fernando Hierro.

588
00:40:08.480 --> 00:40:09.320
FLORENTINO SIGNS FIGO

589
00:40:12.360 --> 00:40:13.640
WAR OVER FIGO

590
00:40:15.400 --> 00:40:17.200
To be honest, I didn't believe it.

591
00:40:17.280 --> 00:40:18.120
No.

592
00:40:20.600 --> 00:40:22.720
The precontract was such a big deal.

593
00:40:22.800 --> 00:40:25.200
Everyone knew what his release clause was

594
00:40:25.280 --> 00:40:28.400
and that it would be activated
if Florentino won the elections.

595
00:40:29.280 --> 00:40:32.120
And, personally,
I thought it was impossible.

596
00:40:33.600 --> 00:40:36.440
[in Spanish] The Portuguese player's agent
admits there has been contact,

597
00:40:36.520 --> 00:40:39.000
but as of now,
Pérez is silent on the matter,

598
00:40:39.080 --> 00:40:40.920
although he doesn't deny the news.

599
00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:44.720
[Spanish] If I'm president of Real Madrid,
the best players will play for Madrid.

600
00:40:44.800 --> 00:40:47.400
[reporter, in Spanish] So you don't deny
an agreement's been signed?

601
00:40:47.480 --> 00:40:49.520
What I don't deny
is that if I'm president,

602
00:40:49.600 --> 00:40:51.360
Madrid will have the best players.

603
00:40:52.880 --> 00:40:54.720
[reporter 1, in Spanish]
Figo's agent was more forthcoming

604
00:40:54.800 --> 00:40:57.040
and admits being in contact
with Florentino Pérez.

605
00:40:57.120 --> 00:40:59.760
[Veiga, in Spanish]
If he says it's true, then it is.

606
00:40:59.840 --> 00:41:02.160
I had a meeting with him last week.

607
00:41:02.240 --> 00:41:05.920
This is now public knowledge,
and Florentino knows what he's saying.

608
00:41:06.000 --> 00:41:09.120
And if he's saying it,
it's because he can do it.

609
00:41:09.200 --> 00:41:11.600
Contracts are there to be respected.

610
00:41:11.680 --> 00:41:15.440
[reporter 2, in Catalan] However,
the Barcelona candidates don't believe it.

611
00:41:16.320 --> 00:41:19.760
[in Catalan] Figo hasn't authorized
any contract to be signed on his behalf.

612
00:41:19.840 --> 00:41:25.800
But if they're reckless enough,
and I'm sure they're not, uh,

613
00:41:25.880 --> 00:41:32.560
to sign any kind of document,
then that contract is completely illegal.

614
00:41:32.640 --> 00:41:36.840
[in Catalan] I'll explain it very quickly
for those who haven't read MARCA.

615
00:41:36.920 --> 00:41:39.560
It says that on 1st July,
a document was signed

616
00:41:39.640 --> 00:41:41.280
between Veiga and Florentino Pérez.

617
00:41:41.360 --> 00:41:43.400
Mr. Gaspart says this document is illegal,

618
00:41:43.480 --> 00:41:45.920
but MARCA editors claim
they've seen Veiga's signature.

619
00:41:48.280 --> 00:41:50.800
The worst thing about the Luís Figo saga,

620
00:41:50.880 --> 00:41:53.680
which is where the word "betrayal"
comes into it,

621
00:41:53.760 --> 00:41:55.720
is that, according to Figo,

622
00:41:56.440 --> 00:41:59.600
Veiga signed a contract
without his knowledge.

623
00:41:59.680 --> 00:42:00.760
I don't believe him.

624
00:42:06.960 --> 00:42:10.560
How can an agent do that
without the verbal consent of his player?

625
00:42:12.400 --> 00:42:15.320
Luís Figo has denied this contract
for a long time,

626
00:42:16.000 --> 00:42:18.080
and in his version of events,

627
00:42:18.160 --> 00:42:22.520
he claims he didn't know anything,
that it was something his agent had done,

628
00:42:22.600 --> 00:42:24.680
and he had no knowledge of that contract.

629
00:42:27.400 --> 00:42:28.560
What precontract?

630
00:42:33.880 --> 00:42:36.000
Look, all I can tell you is my truth.

631
00:42:36.840 --> 00:42:37.760
Um…

632
00:42:40.320 --> 00:42:43.240
I think that the only person
who can really respond to this

633
00:42:43.320 --> 00:42:44.160
is José,

634
00:42:46.760 --> 00:42:49.520
who is the one that,
theoretically, signed the contract.

635
00:42:55.040 --> 00:42:57.440
The only thing I did was say to José,

636
00:42:57.520 --> 00:43:00.600
"Look, you talk to whoever you need to,

637
00:43:00.680 --> 00:43:03.160
and then we can decide
if this is real or not."

638
00:43:05.040 --> 00:43:07.640
So I honestly don't know
if anyone signed a contract

639
00:43:07.720 --> 00:43:08.920
because I never saw it.

640
00:43:11.560 --> 00:43:13.360
[interviewer] Was there a precontract?

641
00:43:14.680 --> 00:43:15.640
There was, yes.

642
00:43:16.800 --> 00:43:19.280
-[interviewer] Did you sign it?
-Yes, I signed it.

643
00:43:20.000 --> 00:43:21.880
-[interviewer] Did Figo sign it?
-No.

644
00:43:21.960 --> 00:43:24.360
No, Figo didn't sign it. He was unable to.

645
00:43:25.160 --> 00:43:27.520
[interviewer] Did Figo ask you
to sign the contract?

646
00:43:27.600 --> 00:43:28.440
Yes.

647
00:43:29.880 --> 00:43:32.480
One thing is me telling him
to speak to people,

648
00:43:32.560 --> 00:43:35.440
but it's another thing
if he signs something on my behalf.

649
00:43:38.520 --> 00:43:41.360
If he signed it,
then he was making the commitment,

650
00:43:41.440 --> 00:43:44.000
and he was taking the risks
in this situation.

651
00:43:45.440 --> 00:43:48.200
Because he didn't really have
any way of making me responsible

652
00:43:48.280 --> 00:43:49.800
for a situation like this.

653
00:43:55.360 --> 00:43:58.840
[Veiga] It's not in my interest to lie.
Twenty-one years have gone by.

654
00:43:58.920 --> 00:44:02.040
But I think now's the time
for me to tell my side of the story.

655
00:44:03.480 --> 00:44:05.760
Luís Figo never saw that contract.

656
00:44:05.840 --> 00:44:07.040
He never saw it.

657
00:44:07.120 --> 00:44:11.240
Florentino Pérez never had a copy.
There was only one version of it.

658
00:44:12.280 --> 00:44:14.000
And before signing the contract,

659
00:44:14.520 --> 00:44:16.000
I called Luís Figo

660
00:44:16.680 --> 00:44:18.720
and read him out the contract in full.

661
00:44:24.600 --> 00:44:25.600
And I asked him,

662
00:44:26.280 --> 00:44:27.760
"Luís, can I sign it?"

663
00:44:32.200 --> 00:44:34.320
And Luís replied, "Yes, you can."

664
00:44:34.400 --> 00:44:35.760
So I signed it.

665
00:44:35.840 --> 00:44:38.600
It was impossible
for me to sign any document

666
00:44:38.680 --> 00:44:40.440
without the consent of the player,

667
00:44:40.520 --> 00:44:42.560
be it Figo or anyone else.

668
00:44:42.640 --> 00:44:43.560
Impossible.

669
00:44:46.640 --> 00:44:48.920
[reporter, in Spanish]
Lorenzo Sanz doesn't believe it.

670
00:44:49.000 --> 00:44:52.040
For the time being, he's demanding
respect for the Real Madrid squad

671
00:44:52.120 --> 00:44:56.080
and thinks Figo's agent,
José Veiga, should not be trusted.

672
00:44:56.160 --> 00:44:59.960
[in Spanish] It's a worthless
piece of paper. He doesn't know football.

673
00:45:00.040 --> 00:45:04.720
If you trust an agent capable
of signing contracts with different clubs…

674
00:45:04.800 --> 00:45:06.080
Juve, Parma…

675
00:45:06.160 --> 00:45:08.960
it seems to me
you don't understand football.

676
00:45:10.280 --> 00:45:14.240
5 YEARS EARLIER

677
00:45:16.160 --> 00:45:18.160
[commentator speaking in Portuguese]

678
00:45:26.520 --> 00:45:28.960
[Veiga] I met him when he was 16 or 17.

679
00:45:29.040 --> 00:45:30.760
We started to work together then.

680
00:45:33.320 --> 00:45:37.960
Luís Figo was already at such a high level
that his future was destined to be abroad.

681
00:45:39.960 --> 00:45:42.120
[reporter, in Portuguese]
A Portuguese name in the news,

682
00:45:42.200 --> 00:45:45.360
and it's Sporting Lisbon player
Luís Figo, in a tug-of-war

683
00:45:45.440 --> 00:45:46.840
between Parma and Juventus.

684
00:45:47.680 --> 00:45:50.480
Figo's departure from Sporting
is a real soap opera,

685
00:45:50.560 --> 00:45:53.240
and it's still not known
where the player will end up.

686
00:45:55.520 --> 00:45:57.320
We're talking about the '90s,

687
00:45:57.400 --> 00:45:59.960
and Italian football
was the best in the world.

688
00:46:00.040 --> 00:46:02.520
So every player wanted to play in Italy.

689
00:46:02.600 --> 00:46:07.240
[in Portuguese] Figo signed for Parma
this morning, in an office here in Lisbon.

690
00:46:07.320 --> 00:46:10.160
[reporter 2, in Portuguese]
By midday, he'd signed on the dotted line,

691
00:46:10.240 --> 00:46:13.880
and the handshakes see him
join the club for the next three years.

692
00:46:13.960 --> 00:46:17.160
Parma has beaten Juventus,
at least in winning Figo over.

693
00:46:18.280 --> 00:46:21.600
But Juventus didn't give up,
and they signed an agreement

694
00:46:21.680 --> 00:46:22.560
with Luís Figo.

695
00:46:24.480 --> 00:46:27.720
[Portuguese] Parma and Juventus are trying
to determine Figo's final destination.

696
00:46:27.800 --> 00:46:30.280
It was a tough meeting,
on a day the paper O Jogo

697
00:46:30.360 --> 00:46:34.360
revealed fresh accusations
against the player's agent, José Veiga.

698
00:46:35.240 --> 00:46:38.320
They convinced him
to sign the agreement without me knowing.

699
00:46:39.480 --> 00:46:43.360
[reporter 3, in Portuguese]
Veiga slipped up in a recent letter.

700
00:46:43.440 --> 00:46:46.680
First he refers to the document
signed between Figo and Juventus

701
00:46:46.760 --> 00:46:47.800
as an "agreement."

702
00:46:47.880 --> 00:46:50.520
But in the second paragraph,
he refers to it as a "contract."

703
00:46:50.600 --> 00:46:53.280
The agent
unintentionally recognized that Figo,

704
00:46:53.360 --> 00:46:56.160
instead of signing a pre-agreement,

705
00:46:56.240 --> 00:47:00.720
had signed a real contract with Turin.
The contradictions are obvious.

706
00:47:01.920 --> 00:47:04.080
[reporter in Portuguese]
Are you aware that Juventus

707
00:47:04.160 --> 00:47:08.120
could put pressure on the authorities,
and you'll be unable to play in Italy?

708
00:47:08.200 --> 00:47:09.320
Are you aware of this?

709
00:47:10.240 --> 00:47:15.480
[in Portuguese] No, because I only signed
a valid contract with Parma.

710
00:47:15.560 --> 00:47:18.600
-[reporter] Are you sure?
-As far as I know, that's the case.

711
00:47:18.680 --> 00:47:23.680
-Did you sign a contract with Juventus?
-I didn't. I signed an agreement.

712
00:47:24.480 --> 00:47:26.600
I've already said this several times.

713
00:47:26.680 --> 00:47:29.320
Uh, the only contract I had
was with my agent,

714
00:47:29.400 --> 00:47:31.600
and I'll honor it.

715
00:47:38.040 --> 00:47:41.720
[anchor, in Portuguese] Juventus and Parma
have given up on signing Luís Figo.

716
00:47:41.800 --> 00:47:45.720
The two clubs
met with the Italian Football Federation,

717
00:47:45.800 --> 00:47:49.200
and the player is banned from playing
in Italy for the next two years.

718
00:47:49.280 --> 00:47:52.040
[in Portuguese] Banned from playing
in Italy for two years,

719
00:47:52.120 --> 00:47:56.360
he must be loaned by Parma
to another club, possibly in Spain.

720
00:47:56.440 --> 00:47:58.360
[in Portuguese]
Luís Figo is already in Barcelona.

721
00:47:58.440 --> 00:48:00.520
The Portuguese player arrived

722
00:48:00.600 --> 00:48:02.920
in the Catalan capital yesterday.

723
00:48:03.000 --> 00:48:06.640
[reporter, in Portuguese] Champagne
and olés all round for Barça's new star,

724
00:48:06.720 --> 00:48:08.960
greeted by a legion of fans.

725
00:48:12.720 --> 00:48:16.680
7 DAYS TO THE ELECTIONS

726
00:48:17.800 --> 00:48:19.680
[telephone rings, clicks]

727
00:48:19.760 --> 00:48:22.640
[Figo, in Spanish]
Hello! I'm busy at the moment,

728
00:48:22.720 --> 00:48:25.840
possibly doing something more interesting.

729
00:48:25.920 --> 00:48:26.760
Oops!

730
00:48:27.800 --> 00:48:30.000
Leave a message after the beep.

731
00:48:30.080 --> 00:48:31.160
Thanks.

732
00:48:37.440 --> 00:48:41.680
[in Spanish] Luís Figo has become the
focal point of the Real Madrid elections.

733
00:48:41.760 --> 00:48:45.840
Pérez hasn't confirmed or denied
having an agreement with the player.

734
00:48:45.920 --> 00:48:49.880
And Figo, who we were with
this morning in the Algarve,

735
00:48:49.960 --> 00:48:51.920
also doesn't deny the news.

736
00:48:52.880 --> 00:48:55.400
[Figo, in Spanish] Sorry you guys
came all this way, but

737
00:48:55.920 --> 00:48:57.600
I don't have anything to say.

738
00:48:57.680 --> 00:48:59.800
[reporter, in Spanish]
Can you confirm or deny the news?

739
00:48:59.880 --> 00:49:02.240
No. Sorry. Sorry.

740
00:49:09.560 --> 00:49:10.960
[Futre] I was always by his side.

741
00:49:11.040 --> 00:49:14.240
I was with him in the Algarve
every day, calming him down.

742
00:49:16.000 --> 00:49:17.640
And trying to keep him positive.

743
00:49:28.000 --> 00:49:30.080
I'd had dinner with him the night before.

744
00:49:31.280 --> 00:49:33.440
I'd been with him,
and he didn't say a word.

745
00:49:43.920 --> 00:49:47.760
I wake up, and when I switch on my phone,
my inbox is full of messages.

746
00:49:47.840 --> 00:49:49.840
From Florentino Pérez,

747
00:49:50.400 --> 00:49:51.440
José Veiga…

748
00:49:51.960 --> 00:49:52.880
[electronic beep]

749
00:49:52.960 --> 00:49:55.240
[Futre] "Paulo…" [echoes]

750
00:49:55.840 --> 00:49:58.400
[electronic beeping]

751
00:49:58.480 --> 00:50:01.840
FIGO DENIES EVERYTHING

752
00:50:01.920 --> 00:50:04.480
[in Spanish] In an interview
with the Catalan newspaper SPORT,

753
00:50:04.560 --> 00:50:06.160
Figo says he will stay with Barça.

754
00:50:06.240 --> 00:50:10.360
Total madness on this Sunday
during the campaign.

755
00:50:10.440 --> 00:50:13.000
[reporter 1, in Spanish] Figo's bombshell
has forced the candidates

756
00:50:13.080 --> 00:50:14.720
to take unexpected measures.

757
00:50:14.800 --> 00:50:17.000
Florentino Pérez had to stop by his tent

758
00:50:17.080 --> 00:50:20.200
to try to explain
the Portuguese player's statement.

759
00:50:20.280 --> 00:50:23.240
Lorenzo Sanz
bumped up his flight from Barcelona

760
00:50:23.320 --> 00:50:26.240
to attend a press conference
at his campaign headquarters.

761
00:50:26.320 --> 00:50:28.680
[in Spanish] He must realize now
that he can't keep lying,

762
00:50:28.760 --> 00:50:30.440
and this is now falling apart for him.

763
00:50:30.520 --> 00:50:33.600
[in Spanish] Do I look worried?
I am calm. Relax.

764
00:50:34.160 --> 00:50:35.960
"Tranquil," as the Catalonians say.

765
00:50:36.040 --> 00:50:39.080
REAL MADRID PRESIDENTIAL CAMPAIGN
FLORENTINO PÉREZ

766
00:50:42.600 --> 00:50:45.960
[Veiga] When this interview came out,
Florentino Pérez called me.

767
00:50:48.040 --> 00:50:49.920
"José, what's this interview about?"

768
00:50:50.000 --> 00:50:52.360
"How can this be possible?
This can't happen."

769
00:50:52.440 --> 00:50:55.080
"We're in the middle of an election.
What's going on?"

770
00:50:55.160 --> 00:50:56.440
And I calmed him down.

771
00:50:58.480 --> 00:51:00.280
"No, Florentino, it's all good."

772
00:51:00.360 --> 00:51:03.600
"There's no problem.
It's just pressure coming from Barcelona."

773
00:51:03.680 --> 00:51:05.520
"Don't worry. It's all going well."

774
00:51:07.920 --> 00:51:10.240
And Florentino said,
"That's all well and good,

775
00:51:10.320 --> 00:51:12.600
but now he has to
do an interview with MARCA."

776
00:51:13.680 --> 00:51:17.600
6 DAYS TO THE ELECTIONS

777
00:51:18.200 --> 00:51:20.680
[anchor, in Spanish] The Figo case
continues to grab headlines.

778
00:51:20.760 --> 00:51:25.040
Today, MARCA published a story
that contradicts yesterday's SPORT piece.

779
00:51:25.120 --> 00:51:26.920
FLORENTINO HAS HIM SIGNED

780
00:51:27.000 --> 00:51:28.760
FIGO: THE WHOLE TRUTH

781
00:51:29.800 --> 00:51:31.920
On MARCA's front page, he said,

782
00:51:32.960 --> 00:51:33.960
"If he wins,

783
00:51:34.880 --> 00:51:36.280
who knows what will happen?"

784
00:51:37.000 --> 00:51:39.800
He'd said he would never wear
the Real Madrid shirt,

785
00:51:40.800 --> 00:51:42.360
and then the next day, he said,

786
00:51:43.040 --> 00:51:43.880
"Maybe."

787
00:51:44.960 --> 00:51:48.640
[reporter, in Spanish] Tomorrow,
Florentino Pérez will address the issue.

788
00:51:48.720 --> 00:51:50.800
But in the meantime, who should we trust?

789
00:51:50.880 --> 00:51:52.840
[in Spanish] Personally, I trust MARCA.

790
00:51:54.760 --> 00:51:56.680
Without a shadow of a doubt.

791
00:51:56.760 --> 00:51:57.600
Poor Luís Figo.

792
00:51:57.680 --> 00:52:00.120
He's been under
a lot of pressure this week.

793
00:52:00.200 --> 00:52:02.400
It wouldn't shock me if he loses it a bit.

794
00:52:02.480 --> 00:52:04.600
I don't pay attention to rumors.

795
00:52:04.680 --> 00:52:07.800
Tomorrow, I'll talk about my plans,

796
00:52:07.880 --> 00:52:11.480
and I'll also talk about Luís Figo,
and I'd like it to be the last time.

797
00:52:14.560 --> 00:52:18.520
5 DAYS TO THE ELECTIONS

798
00:52:18.600 --> 00:52:21.040
THIS IS HOW MADRID WINS

799
00:52:21.800 --> 00:52:25.920
[Pérez, in Spanish] I would ask that the
members not talk about this issue anymore.

800
00:52:26.760 --> 00:52:29.000
If I become president of Real Madrid,

801
00:52:29.080 --> 00:52:29.920
Luís Figo

802
00:52:30.760 --> 00:52:33.320
will be a Real Madrid player.

803
00:52:34.800 --> 00:52:37.120
And to underline how confident I am,

804
00:52:38.640 --> 00:52:41.400
if I am elected president
and this doesn't happen,

805
00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:47.360
I will pay the membership fees
for every member next season.

806
00:52:47.440 --> 00:52:49.320
[crowd applauds, whistles]

807
00:52:59.680 --> 00:53:02.320
[Díaz] This was the moment
when all Real Madrid members were saying,

808
00:53:02.400 --> 00:53:04.320
"This is actually serious. It's real."

809
00:53:07.480 --> 00:53:10.320
"And here's a president who can
make us dream more than the other guy,

810
00:53:10.400 --> 00:53:12.760
who'd just won two Champions Leagues."

811
00:53:13.360 --> 00:53:16.360
[crowd applauds, cheers, whistles]

812
00:53:16.440 --> 00:53:19.600
[Sanz, in Spanish] We'll see tomorrow
when Mr. Figo denies it again,

813
00:53:19.680 --> 00:53:23.880
and I hope this time it'll be definitive
that he's staying with Barcelona

814
00:53:23.960 --> 00:53:26.160
and that he apologizes to the members.

815
00:53:26.240 --> 00:53:30.120
[reporter, in Spanish] Lorenzo Sanz's team
is ready to counter the Figo effect,

816
00:53:30.200 --> 00:53:34.000
and there's nothing better
than showing Figo at his most Barcelona.

817
00:53:34.080 --> 00:53:36.840
All members will receive
a copy of this video.

818
00:53:36.920 --> 00:53:40.120
[chants in Spanish] Madrid crybabies!
Bow down to the champions!

819
00:53:40.200 --> 00:53:43.280
Madrid crybabies!
Bow down to the champions!

820
00:53:43.360 --> 00:53:44.720
Long live Barça!

821
00:53:44.800 --> 00:53:46.800
[crowd cheering]

822
00:53:50.040 --> 00:53:52.560
[in Spanish] As his teammate, as a fan,

823
00:53:52.640 --> 00:53:56.560
knowing how great a footballer he is,
I hope he stays at Barcelona.

824
00:53:56.640 --> 00:53:58.720
That's what me and all the fans hope for.

825
00:53:58.800 --> 00:54:02.280
Obviously, it's his decision,
and he needs time to think it through.

826
00:54:02.360 --> 00:54:08.080
I know him, and I know
he doesn't take these decisions lightly.

827
00:54:09.640 --> 00:54:11.080
We talked about it,

828
00:54:11.160 --> 00:54:13.240
and I gave him my opinion as a friend.

829
00:54:16.040 --> 00:54:19.440
He said he had to think about it.
That he'd had an offer from Madrid,

830
00:54:19.520 --> 00:54:20.880
and he'd take a look at it.

831
00:54:23.280 --> 00:54:25.560
I definitely tried
to convince him to stay.

832
00:54:25.640 --> 00:54:29.120
That there was no better place to be.
That the people here loved him.

833
00:54:29.200 --> 00:54:30.360
And he knew it.

834
00:54:30.440 --> 00:54:33.480
And that he'd be a unique
and once-in-a-lifetime player here.

835
00:54:35.240 --> 00:54:37.240
[stopwatch ticking]

836
00:54:40.400 --> 00:54:42.400
[Guardiola] Barcelona's a city he loved.

837
00:54:44.640 --> 00:54:46.720
[interviewer, in Spanish]
Why's Barça more than a club?

838
00:54:48.880 --> 00:54:51.040
If you think that it is. [chuckles]

839
00:54:51.120 --> 00:54:53.600
[in Spanish] Yes, when you're here,
you realize it is…

840
00:54:53.680 --> 00:54:55.920
SPEAKING IN 1999

841
00:54:56.000 --> 00:54:58.800
…because of the affection of the people.

842
00:54:58.880 --> 00:55:00.480
I believe that, uh,

843
00:55:00.560 --> 00:55:05.320
a club can't just, uh, be about sports.

844
00:55:05.400 --> 00:55:09.640
I feel like I'm at home,

845
00:55:09.720 --> 00:55:11.160
uh, with a family.

846
00:55:11.680 --> 00:55:16.120
Also, because of the club's past
during Franco's dictatorship.

847
00:55:16.680 --> 00:55:22.280
And so, for all those reasons, uh,
you can say that it's more than a club.

848
00:55:25.920 --> 00:55:28.000
[narrator, in English]
Barcelona, capital of Catalonia,

849
00:55:28.080 --> 00:55:30.840
suffers its last bombardment
before capture by Franco's army.

850
00:55:46.680 --> 00:55:49.240
[Guardiola] When speaking Catalan
was banned in Barcelona

851
00:55:49.320 --> 00:55:50.720
during the Franco era,

852
00:55:50.800 --> 00:55:52.840
and our language was persecuted,

853
00:55:53.440 --> 00:55:56.520
the Nou Camp was a place
where you could express yourself

854
00:55:57.040 --> 00:55:58.120
with total freedom.

855
00:56:04.720 --> 00:56:07.200
For me, it's clear,
Barça's more than a club.

856
00:56:09.960 --> 00:56:11.960
Barça is a Catalan club.

857
00:56:12.040 --> 00:56:13.760
Very pro-Catalonia.

858
00:56:13.840 --> 00:56:15.400
Rooted in the region.

859
00:56:15.480 --> 00:56:16.360
In our land.

860
00:56:19.920 --> 00:56:25.200
And it obviously brings together
who we are and what we represent,

861
00:56:26.240 --> 00:56:28.760
which is our country and our feelings.

862
00:56:33.120 --> 00:56:36.280
This is why the symbolism
of what Barça means to Catalonia,

863
00:56:36.360 --> 00:56:38.640
and vice versa, cannot be separated.

864
00:56:38.720 --> 00:56:41.320
And as a football club,
it's one of the biggest.

865
00:56:41.400 --> 00:56:43.240
For some of us, it is the biggest.

866
00:56:44.760 --> 00:56:47.120
[commentator speaking in Spanish]

867
00:56:48.480 --> 00:56:50.640
[commentator shouts enthusiastically]

868
00:56:51.320 --> 00:56:53.360
[commentator speaking in Catalan]

869
00:56:53.440 --> 00:56:55.440
[commentator yelling passionately]

870
00:56:58.720 --> 00:57:00.720
[commentator speaking in Spanish]

871
00:57:13.200 --> 00:57:16.160
Barcelona being more than a club
means just that.

872
00:57:17.080 --> 00:57:20.520
We're representatives
of a very specific way of being,

873
00:57:21.400 --> 00:57:23.320
which is against centralism.

874
00:57:25.320 --> 00:57:28.200
So, if Real Madrid represents centralism,

875
00:57:28.280 --> 00:57:30.640
then the conditions are perfect
for the rivalry.

876
00:57:33.280 --> 00:57:37.080
[interviewer, in Spanish]
You know that the Catalan people

877
00:57:37.160 --> 00:57:39.160
express their feelings through this club

878
00:57:39.240 --> 00:57:42.080
to Spain and the rest of the world.

879
00:57:42.600 --> 00:57:45.960
That's how we express Catalan nationalism.
What do you think about this?

880
00:57:47.400 --> 00:57:51.160
From the outside, from my point of view,

881
00:57:51.240 --> 00:57:55.880
it's a way to reclaim, um,

882
00:57:57.120 --> 00:58:02.640
a way of life, a way of thinking,

883
00:58:02.720 --> 00:58:04.880
for the people of Catalonia.

884
00:58:04.960 --> 00:58:08.680
Since I arrived at the club,
I've always felt supported.

885
00:58:09.200 --> 00:58:13.360
I think I owe the people
a debt of gratitude.

886
00:58:13.440 --> 00:58:15.040
We're a family!

887
00:58:15.120 --> 00:58:16.680
[crowd cheers raucously]

888
00:58:16.760 --> 00:58:19.040
-[in Catalan] Long live Barça!
-[crowd cheers]

889
00:58:19.120 --> 00:58:20.280
Long live Catalonia!

890
00:58:23.080 --> 00:58:24.760
[air horns honk enthusiastically]

891
00:58:25.400 --> 00:58:28.040
[Figo, present] I identified
with the values of the club.

892
00:58:29.880 --> 00:58:31.120
I defended them to the death.

893
00:58:32.880 --> 00:58:34.200
I was seen as one of them.

894
00:58:38.440 --> 00:58:42.400
2 DAYS TO THE ELECTIONS

895
00:58:45.240 --> 00:58:48.520
[in Spanish] We have exclusive footage
shot by a TeleMadrid camera

896
00:58:48.600 --> 00:58:51.800
of an event that occurred this afternoon
at Hotel Meliá Castilla.

897
00:58:51.880 --> 00:58:56.720
In it, Florentino Pérez
is meeting with José Veiga,

898
00:58:56.800 --> 00:58:59.280
the agent of the Portuguese player

899
00:58:59.360 --> 00:59:03.800
who Madrid fans would love to see join
but who still belongs to Barcelona.

900
00:59:04.400 --> 00:59:07.360
This is a preview of the meeting.
Listen to what Veiga says.

901
00:59:07.440 --> 00:59:11.160
[in Spanish] We hope Florentino wins.
If he wins, we'll be here on Monday.

902
00:59:11.680 --> 00:59:14.120
[anchor] "If Florentino wins,
we'll be here on Monday."

903
00:59:14.200 --> 00:59:17.960
He's referring to himself
and his client, Luís Figo.

904
00:59:20.240 --> 00:59:22.280
[Veiga, present] I felt Florentino
was very confident.

905
00:59:22.960 --> 00:59:26.320
And he knew if he could deliver Figo,
he'd win the elections.

906
00:59:32.040 --> 00:59:33.720
But Luís had many doubts.

907
00:59:34.240 --> 00:59:37.200
He felt that staying in Barcelona
could be for the best.

908
00:59:39.160 --> 00:59:40.160
It was really tough.

909
00:59:41.800 --> 00:59:45.480
[in Spanish] We don't want him here.
He can go. They can pay his buyout clause.

910
00:59:45.560 --> 00:59:48.520
[in Spanish] He's a mercenary.
He can go to hell.

911
00:59:49.280 --> 00:59:50.360
Got that? Period.

912
00:59:53.760 --> 00:59:56.280
[Figo, chants softly in Spanish]
We're in Sardinia!

913
00:59:59.800 --> 01:00:02.520
We've come to spend a few days here.

914
01:00:08.600 --> 01:00:11.240
[Figo] Throughout the process,
there were moments of doubt.

915
01:00:11.320 --> 01:00:13.240
Of thinking "yes," then thinking "no."

916
01:00:17.680 --> 01:00:19.080
There were a lot of threats,

917
01:00:20.680 --> 01:00:21.720
a lot of pressure,

918
01:00:22.600 --> 01:00:25.360
a lot of nasty statements and stories,

919
01:00:25.440 --> 01:00:27.720
not just against me but against my family.

920
01:00:30.760 --> 01:00:34.280
Switching to play for your archrivals
is not an easy decision.

921
01:00:41.280 --> 01:00:43.040
[phone ringing]

922
01:00:43.880 --> 01:00:45.880
[woman and child softly singing]

923
01:00:46.760 --> 01:00:48.280
[man] Luís Figo called me to say,

924
01:00:48.360 --> 01:00:52.480
"We have to put an end to all the rumors
because it's really damaging for me."

925
01:00:52.560 --> 01:00:56.520
"I'm getting crucified in Barcelona,
and I'd like to clear a few things up."

926
01:00:57.200 --> 01:00:59.160
-[Figo laughs]
-[child, in Spanish] Yes!

927
01:01:00.240 --> 01:01:03.240
[Frieros] SPORT travelled to Sardinia,
to the Romazzino Hotel

928
01:01:03.320 --> 01:01:04.560
on the Costa Smeralda.

929
01:01:05.920 --> 01:01:07.640
Nobody held a gun to his head.

930
01:01:08.160 --> 01:01:10.640
He was free to say and do
what he thought best.

931
01:01:11.240 --> 01:01:14.280
And he was convinced
that he'd stay at Barcelona

932
01:01:14.360 --> 01:01:16.320
whether Florentino won or lost.

933
01:01:26.080 --> 01:01:28.080
[dramatic electronic music plays]

934
01:01:33.840 --> 01:01:35.760
NO TO MADRID

935
01:01:35.840 --> 01:01:38.040
"I WILL STAY WITH BARÇA…"

936
01:01:38.840 --> 01:01:41.560
[Frieros] "It has come to the point,
driven by the circumstances,

937
01:01:41.640 --> 01:01:43.760
when he can no longer remain indifferent."

938
01:01:45.120 --> 01:01:47.960
"Figo wants to put an end
to the summer soap opera."

939
01:01:48.560 --> 01:01:50.400
"'You won't go to Real Madrid?'"

940
01:01:50.480 --> 01:01:51.720
"'No, I won't go.'"

941
01:01:51.800 --> 01:01:53.200
"'You'll stay at Barça?'"

942
01:01:54.800 --> 01:01:57.720
"'That's always been my intention,
my desire, and my hope,

943
01:01:57.800 --> 01:01:59.240
since the beginning.'"

944
01:01:59.320 --> 01:02:00.680
"'I will not leave Barça.'"

945
01:02:01.200 --> 01:02:02.840
"'That is my final decision.'"

946
01:02:03.920 --> 01:02:05.880
"Luís Figo picks up a Barça shirt."

947
01:02:05.960 --> 01:02:07.800
"It's his. The number seven."

948
01:02:07.880 --> 01:02:10.280
"He puts it on, and the matter is closed."

949
01:02:10.360 --> 01:02:12.680
"THIS IS AND WILL CONTINUE TO BE MY SHIRT"

950
01:02:20.000 --> 01:02:23.880
I'm convinced that if he said he'd stay,
it's because he thought he'd stay.

951
01:02:24.880 --> 01:02:26.880
I don't think it's a case of him saying,

952
01:02:26.960 --> 01:02:28.280
"I'm going to Real Madrid,

953
01:02:28.360 --> 01:02:30.920
but I'm going to say I'll stay
when I know I'm not."

954
01:02:31.560 --> 01:02:33.960
That's not very smart,
and Luís is a clever guy.

955
01:02:37.920 --> 01:02:40.320
[interviewer] When you were pictured
in a Barça shirt,

956
01:02:40.840 --> 01:02:42.680
did you really believe you were staying?

957
01:02:46.880 --> 01:02:48.560
Yes, at the time, I thought so.

958
01:02:49.640 --> 01:02:53.040
I thought that was going to happen.
That's why I did it.

959
01:02:58.120 --> 01:02:59.840
[stopwatch ticking]

960
01:02:59.920 --> 01:03:04.040
ELECTION DAY

961
01:03:09.320 --> 01:03:11.320
[dramatic electronic music plays]

962
01:03:11.400 --> 01:03:13.400
[unheard dialogue]

963
01:03:16.760 --> 01:03:19.720
-[in Spanish] I've not slept at all.
-[Spanish reporter] You couldn't sleep?

964
01:03:19.800 --> 01:03:21.520
-Did you try?
-Not at all.

965
01:03:21.600 --> 01:03:23.560
-[reporter] Did you shower?
-I did take a shower.

966
01:03:23.640 --> 01:03:25.600
[indistinct chatter]

967
01:03:30.880 --> 01:03:34.080
[in Spanish] Now onto sports news.
Real Madrid remains in the spotlight.

968
01:03:34.160 --> 01:03:37.520
-We're joined by Roberto Gómez.
-[in Spanish] Hello, everyone, Isabel.

969
01:03:37.600 --> 01:03:42.760
Yes, Real Madrid is in the spotlight
because the club has a new president.

970
01:03:42.840 --> 01:03:44.840
[stopwatch ticking]

971
01:03:53.480 --> 01:03:55.480
[dramatic electronic music plays]

972
01:03:58.680 --> 01:04:01.480
[interviewer] The story of this transfer
is one where everyone claims

973
01:04:01.560 --> 01:04:03.000
to be telling the truth.

974
01:04:03.080 --> 01:04:05.680
Who do you think
is telling the actual truth?

975
01:04:08.000 --> 01:04:10.040
I am. Because I'm the protagonist.

976
01:04:10.120 --> 01:04:12.280
Everything that I tell you
is what happened.

977
01:04:14.960 --> 01:04:16.840
[unheard dialogue]

978
01:04:16.920 --> 01:04:21.400
[in Spanish] Between us,
we'll ensure that the name of this club

979
01:04:21.480 --> 01:04:23.480
is synonymous with greatness.

980
01:04:23.560 --> 01:04:27.040
Because its history deserves it,
its members deserve it,

981
01:04:27.120 --> 01:04:29.520
as do the millions of supporters
in this city,

982
01:04:29.600 --> 01:04:32.240
in Spain, and all over the world.

983
01:04:32.320 --> 01:04:33.320
Thank you very much.

984
01:04:38.800 --> 01:04:41.000
[reporter, in Spanish]
Florentino will start work today.

985
01:04:41.080 --> 01:04:44.640
Real Madrid members
now await the arrival of Luís Figo.

986
01:04:48.480 --> 01:04:50.080
[Pérez] I've always been a calm person.

987
01:04:51.240 --> 01:04:54.520
I think about what it is I have to do.
If I really want something,

988
01:04:54.600 --> 01:04:56.720
I'm safe in the knowledge
that I'll get it done.

989
01:04:58.600 --> 01:04:59.920
They were crazy times.

990
01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:03.280
I'd just won the elections.
I had to plan and organize everything.

991
01:05:03.360 --> 01:05:07.920
All the media were talking about Figo,
and I think Figo felt a bit overwhelmed.

992
01:05:10.440 --> 01:05:13.280
But I was so sure that Figo
was coming to Real Madrid,

993
01:05:13.360 --> 01:05:14.880
I didn't give it much thought.

994
01:05:14.960 --> 01:05:17.360
Players join Real Madrid
because they want to.

995
01:05:17.440 --> 01:05:19.960
I was convinced
Figo wanted to come to the club.

996
01:05:21.920 --> 01:05:23.840
[interviewer] You didn't have doubts
at any point?

997
01:05:23.920 --> 01:05:25.840
No. I didn't have any doubts.

998
01:05:27.640 --> 01:05:30.280
[in Spanish] Now let's see
the sports headlines.

999
01:05:30.960 --> 01:05:34.720
SPORT, "Barça fans ask,
'What's going to happen?'"

1000
01:05:34.800 --> 01:05:36.400
"Barça supporter or traitor?"

1001
01:05:36.480 --> 01:05:40.800
AS, "Figo bunkers down
in Sardinia. Hounded."

1002
01:05:43.120 --> 01:05:45.760
[phone ringing]

1003
01:05:49.920 --> 01:05:52.440
Florentino won the elections in Madrid,

1004
01:05:53.320 --> 01:05:55.640
and everyone who was involved
in the operation,

1005
01:05:56.160 --> 01:05:57.720
which included my agent,

1006
01:06:00.080 --> 01:06:02.120
tried to persuade me to make the move.

1007
01:06:04.080 --> 01:06:07.480
[phone ringing]

1008
01:06:09.800 --> 01:06:12.520
So Veiga calls Figo, who's in Sardinia.

1009
01:06:14.000 --> 01:06:15.200
That's when Luís said,

1010
01:06:16.480 --> 01:06:18.160
"I'll never go to Real Madrid."

1011
01:06:21.160 --> 01:06:22.640
[in Portuguese] "Never ever."

1012
01:06:23.720 --> 01:06:26.040
"I'm not going.
I'm not going. I'm not going."

1013
01:06:28.920 --> 01:06:31.600
Then Luís tells Veiga
not to call him again.

1014
01:06:32.680 --> 01:06:34.600
"Leave me alone. Don't call me again."

1015
01:06:35.120 --> 01:06:36.320
"You won't convince me!"

1016
01:06:38.800 --> 01:06:40.120
[cell phone rings]

1017
01:06:41.880 --> 01:06:44.280
[De la Morena] I thought
this could fall through at any moment,

1018
01:06:44.360 --> 01:06:45.840
that Barça could take action.

1019
01:06:47.280 --> 01:06:50.720
But I talked with Florentino,
and he told me that it was a done deal.

1020
01:06:52.200 --> 01:06:54.560
I said, "But it could fail
at the last minute."

1021
01:06:54.640 --> 01:06:58.600
"No, it won't, because I've added
a €30 million penalty clause."

1022
01:06:58.680 --> 01:07:02.840
"And if he wants out of the deal,
he'd have to pay Real Madrid €30 million."

1023
01:07:03.840 --> 01:07:04.800
Fuck.

1024
01:07:08.720 --> 01:07:12.120
[Pérez] I'd never signed anything
like that before, I can assure you.

1025
01:07:12.200 --> 01:07:15.680
This was in 2000. I haven't done
anything like that again since then.

1026
01:07:17.440 --> 01:07:20.320
It was, let's say,
a motivational clause and nothing else.

1027
01:07:23.160 --> 01:07:24.360
Figo never signed it.

1028
01:07:24.960 --> 01:07:27.440
It was a contract that Veiga and I signed,

1029
01:07:28.880 --> 01:07:31.440
which could be seen
more as a declaration of intent

1030
01:07:31.960 --> 01:07:33.000
because José Veiga

1031
01:07:33.080 --> 01:07:36.240
didn't have the authority
to sign anything on Figo's behalf.

1032
01:07:40.880 --> 01:07:42.520
[Futre] It was the final clause.

1033
01:07:43.280 --> 01:07:44.840
[unheard dialogue]

1034
01:07:44.920 --> 01:07:46.440
[Futre] I glanced over it.

1035
01:07:46.520 --> 01:07:48.240
[unheard dialogue]

1036
01:07:49.720 --> 01:07:53.160
And if Luís kept saying to Veiga
that he wasn't going to Real Madrid,

1037
01:07:53.240 --> 01:07:54.800
we had a very big problem.

1038
01:07:57.840 --> 01:07:59.040
A colossal problem.

1039
01:08:05.160 --> 01:08:07.840
And this caused José Veiga a lot of stress

1040
01:08:09.480 --> 01:08:11.120
as his name was on the contract.

1041
01:08:15.680 --> 01:08:18.360
Someone had to pay the €30 million.

1042
01:08:21.520 --> 01:08:23.640
[in Portuguese] "I'm not going.
I'm not going."

1043
01:08:25.840 --> 01:08:28.120
I said to José,
"We've only got one solution."

1044
01:08:29.760 --> 01:08:30.640
"Only one."

1045
01:08:31.720 --> 01:08:32.600
"Not two."

1046
01:08:34.480 --> 01:08:36.240
"And that's to hire a private jet."

1047
01:08:37.400 --> 01:08:40.000
-This is Figo's agent.
-[man] He is?

1048
01:08:41.040 --> 01:08:43.600
You're a MARCA reporter.
You need to pay attention.

1049
01:08:44.640 --> 01:08:46.640
[indistinct dialogue]

1050
01:08:52.800 --> 01:08:55.480
[Futre, present] At 4 or 5 a.m.,
we left for Sardinia.

1051
01:08:57.680 --> 01:08:59.920
After that, the nightmare really began.

1052
01:09:03.800 --> 01:09:05.880
[Veiga] He was at the Hotel Romazzino.

1053
01:09:05.960 --> 01:09:08.120
I called him and said,
"We're in the lobby."

1054
01:09:08.200 --> 01:09:09.360
That was at 9 a.m.

1055
01:09:10.320 --> 01:09:12.840
[interviewer] When they phoned
and said they were there,

1056
01:09:12.920 --> 01:09:13.880
what did you think?

1057
01:09:16.440 --> 01:09:18.120
"What are these guys doing here?"

1058
01:09:21.760 --> 01:09:23.680
[Veiga] I could feel a lot of tension.

1059
01:09:27.000 --> 01:09:29.040
His wife, Helen, was really upset.

1060
01:09:35.160 --> 01:09:37.520
Luís was restless and uneasy.

1061
01:09:43.440 --> 01:09:46.520
[Figo, present] José knew
all about the agreement he'd signed.

1062
01:09:49.000 --> 01:09:50.320
But it was his agreement.

1063
01:09:53.440 --> 01:09:55.840
He was aware of the mess
he'd got himself into.

1064
01:10:02.040 --> 01:10:04.880
So they were there
to make me take full responsibility.

1065
01:10:05.880 --> 01:10:06.960
That's why they came.

1066
01:10:12.960 --> 01:10:16.680
[Futre] "I can't go to Real Madrid.
I can't. My life, my family… I can't."

1067
01:10:18.720 --> 01:10:20.000
It was like that all day.

1068
01:10:21.120 --> 01:10:22.040
All day long.

1069
01:10:22.640 --> 01:10:23.880
First in the restaurant

1070
01:10:24.680 --> 01:10:25.800
and then on the beach.

1071
01:10:27.480 --> 01:10:28.480
The beach!

1072
01:10:29.000 --> 01:10:31.720
We go to the beach.
We've got our suits and ties on.

1073
01:10:31.800 --> 01:10:33.560
"Paulo, why are we on the beach?"

1074
01:10:33.640 --> 01:10:36.320
So we followed them to the beach
in our suits.

1075
01:10:44.320 --> 01:10:46.680
I was told, "Go to Sardinia to find Figo."

1076
01:10:46.760 --> 01:10:48.880
"Okay." I went with a colleague.
A photographer.

1077
01:10:52.680 --> 01:10:55.160
So he'd turn up on the beach
every now and then,

1078
01:10:55.240 --> 01:10:56.800
but it was so tense

1079
01:10:56.880 --> 01:10:59.240
because, at that point,
there were still stories in the news

1080
01:10:59.320 --> 01:11:01.840
saying that he was going to
reject this contract.

1081
01:11:08.200 --> 01:11:11.280
[Futre] And that day was terrible.
Terrible. Really hard.

1082
01:11:14.960 --> 01:11:17.200
I said to him, "Okay, Luís, I understand."

1083
01:11:17.920 --> 01:11:20.000
"But if you don't go,
someone will have to pay

1084
01:11:20.080 --> 01:11:22.320
€30 million to Real Madrid."

1085
01:11:25.480 --> 01:11:27.560
It was the €30 million abyss.

1086
01:11:31.240 --> 01:11:34.080
How do you get out of it?
How do you get out of this hole?

1087
01:11:37.720 --> 01:11:39.400
I say to Luís, "Let's do this…"

1088
01:11:41.280 --> 01:11:43.080
"Let's get a private jet to Lisbon."

1089
01:11:43.840 --> 01:11:47.760
"We'll meet Florentino there,
we'll apologize, you'll get to know him."

1090
01:11:47.840 --> 01:11:48.920
"And you can tell him

1091
01:11:49.000 --> 01:11:51.120
that you don't wanna play
for Real Madrid."

1092
01:11:51.880 --> 01:11:55.400
"If you want, we can have a drink
in the city and get the plane back."

1093
01:11:57.160 --> 01:12:00.520
And then we went to the hotel
where we'd been told Figo was staying.

1094
01:12:01.040 --> 01:12:02.920
The first person to see me was Futre.

1095
01:12:04.440 --> 01:12:07.400
He said, "Félix!
What are you doing here? Get outta here!"

1096
01:12:07.480 --> 01:12:09.640
"If Figo sees you,
he'll kill you. Please!"

1097
01:12:10.400 --> 01:12:13.600
Because Figo was about to leave
and catch a private jet to Lisbon

1098
01:12:15.800 --> 01:12:18.720
because he still wasn't sure
about playing for Real Madrid.

1099
01:12:32.920 --> 01:12:34.400
[Veiga] We all met in Lisbon.

1100
01:12:35.760 --> 01:12:40.000
We got to my office, and Florentino Pérez
was there with his staff.

1101
01:12:45.240 --> 01:12:46.840
[Pérez] I told him about my plan,

1102
01:12:46.920 --> 01:12:49.560
that I wanted to develop
a whole sporting project around him.

1103
01:12:50.160 --> 01:12:53.080
I told him the best players in the world
were going to come.

1104
01:12:53.160 --> 01:12:56.480
That we wanted to create
a magical Madrid in line with its history.

1105
01:12:56.560 --> 01:13:00.320
For me, he was the cornerstone
on which I'd develop the whole project.

1106
01:13:07.240 --> 01:13:10.160
[Futre] At this point,
Luís was very close to being won over.

1107
01:13:10.800 --> 01:13:12.080
I remember saying to him,

1108
01:13:14.080 --> 01:13:15.560
"Speak to Helen. Call Helen."

1109
01:13:19.880 --> 01:13:22.680
[Figo] Everyone was gathered there,
trying to convince me

1110
01:13:24.800 --> 01:13:26.680
I tried to listen to everyone.

1111
01:13:28.480 --> 01:13:29.760
Then I called my wife.

1112
01:13:29.840 --> 01:13:32.160
At two or three in the morning,
I think it was,

1113
01:13:32.240 --> 01:13:35.160
and I woke her up and said,
"Look. I'm going to Madrid."

1114
01:13:38.160 --> 01:13:40.360
He started speaking to Helen, in English.

1115
01:13:41.200 --> 01:13:43.480
And he was just saying,

1116
01:13:43.560 --> 01:13:49.400
"Yes. Yes. Yes. Yes. Yes.
Yes. Yes. Yes. Yes. Yes…"

1117
01:13:50.080 --> 01:13:53.080
When the call ended,
he said, "No, I can't. I can't sign it."

1118
01:14:09.280 --> 01:14:11.040
And then Florentino said to him,

1119
01:14:11.120 --> 01:14:12.360
"You'll be my star."

1120
01:14:15.920 --> 01:14:17.880
"I want you at Real Madrid, Luís."

1121
01:14:18.400 --> 01:14:20.360
"I don't want €30 million. I want you."

1122
01:14:20.440 --> 01:14:23.240
"I want to build the best team
in the world. I want you."

1123
01:14:29.840 --> 01:14:31.560
[Figo] I was the one
with everything to lose

1124
01:14:31.640 --> 01:14:34.080
because I had my life set up in Barcelona.

1125
01:14:38.840 --> 01:14:41.520
For me, it started
as a lack of consideration,

1126
01:14:42.720 --> 01:14:45.960
given what I meant to the club,
what I gave to the club,

1127
01:14:46.040 --> 01:14:48.000
and what I'd done for the club.

1128
01:14:49.840 --> 01:14:53.000
I wanted to play football
in a place where I'd be appreciated.

1129
01:14:56.960 --> 01:14:59.720
That's what convinced me
to join Real Madrid.

1130
01:15:04.240 --> 01:15:06.720
The main reason I left
was because they valued me

1131
01:15:06.800 --> 01:15:08.320
and genuinely wanted me.

1132
01:15:11.480 --> 01:15:13.280
In the end, I thought about myself.

1133
01:15:14.320 --> 01:15:15.320
Uh…

1134
01:15:16.600 --> 01:15:18.360
Was it selfish? Maybe.

1135
01:15:19.320 --> 01:15:20.520
Did I earn more money?

1136
01:15:20.600 --> 01:15:21.600
Yes.

1137
01:15:21.680 --> 01:15:23.640
But I think if I'd stayed at Barcelona,

1138
01:15:23.720 --> 01:15:25.200
I would have earned the same.

1139
01:15:27.960 --> 01:15:31.680
These are important moments
when you have to think about yourself.

1140
01:15:38.560 --> 01:15:41.560
[Veiga] It was already dawn,
the sun was rising,

1141
01:15:43.400 --> 01:15:44.640
and Luís signed.

1142
01:15:49.040 --> 01:15:51.000
-[crowd applauds]
-["Cant del Barça" plays]

1143
01:15:51.080 --> 01:15:53.560
5 DAYS LATER

1144
01:16:01.120 --> 01:16:03.360
So the day came when I became president.

1145
01:16:03.440 --> 01:16:07.560
I became president at 9 p.m.
And I went to celebrate.

1146
01:16:08.320 --> 01:16:10.320
[jovial classical music plays]

1147
01:16:12.240 --> 01:16:14.520
[Gaspart] Everyone was happy
because we'd won.

1148
01:16:16.320 --> 01:16:18.280
Luís Figo then calls me on the phone.

1149
01:16:18.360 --> 01:16:19.600
[phone rings]

1150
01:16:19.680 --> 01:16:22.280
[music distorts and fades]

1151
01:16:22.360 --> 01:16:24.200
[phone rings]

1152
01:16:24.280 --> 01:16:26.640
[Gaspart] He said,
"Hi, Joan. Congratulations."

1153
01:16:26.720 --> 01:16:27.880
"Thank you very much."

1154
01:16:27.960 --> 01:16:28.920
So far, fine.

1155
01:16:29.000 --> 01:16:30.600
I said, "When are you arriving?"

1156
01:16:30.680 --> 01:16:32.360
He said, "That depends on you."

1157
01:16:32.440 --> 01:16:34.840
And this is where
the betrayal comes into it.

1158
01:16:34.920 --> 01:16:36.880
He said, "I've got two tickets."

1159
01:16:36.960 --> 01:16:40.880
"One's from Lisbon to Madrid,
and the other's Lisbon to Barcelona."

1160
01:16:40.960 --> 01:16:44.280
"Whether I'll be using
the Barcelona ticket depends on you."

1161
01:16:44.360 --> 01:16:46.040
I said, "What does it depend on?"

1162
01:16:46.920 --> 01:16:49.160
JULY 24, MONDAY

1163
01:16:49.240 --> 01:16:53.520
[Gaspart, in Spanish] "You have to give me
a bank guarantee for 500 million pesetas."

1164
01:16:53.600 --> 01:16:57.160
BARÇA SUPPORTER OR TRAITOR?

1165
01:16:58.280 --> 01:17:00.840
"Then tomorrow,
you'll pick me up at the airport

1166
01:17:00.920 --> 01:17:03.840
and make a huge public statement
as the new president

1167
01:17:03.920 --> 01:17:05.840
that Figo is staying at Barça."

1168
01:17:07.240 --> 01:17:09.680
[jovial classical music resumes]

1169
01:17:14.200 --> 01:17:16.320
[Gaspart] I said,
"Look, Luís, it's midnight."

1170
01:17:16.400 --> 01:17:18.600
"I can't give you a bank guarantee now."

1171
01:17:21.040 --> 01:17:23.360
[unheard dialogue]

1172
01:17:23.440 --> 01:17:25.760
"You're asking me for the impossible."

1173
01:17:25.840 --> 01:17:27.040
"I'm off to Madrid, then."

1174
01:17:27.120 --> 01:17:28.920
"Okay. Good luck. Have a nice trip."

1175
01:17:29.000 --> 01:17:30.480
"What do you want me to say?"

1176
01:17:34.800 --> 01:17:38.560
That thing about, "I've got two tickets,
one for Madrid, one for Barcelona,"

1177
01:17:38.640 --> 01:17:40.560
that's not something I made up.
He said it.

1178
01:17:43.080 --> 01:17:45.520
If he tells the truth,
not a lie, the truth,

1179
01:17:45.600 --> 01:17:47.720
I'll ask the Barça members to forgive him,

1180
01:17:47.800 --> 01:17:50.320
and we can forget all about
the Luís Figo affair.

1181
01:17:51.840 --> 01:17:54.600
[interviewer] Gaspart said
in several interviews that you called him

1182
01:17:54.680 --> 01:17:56.880
the night he won the elections
in Barcelona,

1183
01:17:56.960 --> 01:18:00.680
and you told him you had two tickets,
one for Barcelona and one for Madrid.

1184
01:18:01.200 --> 01:18:02.800
That's a lie. A lie.

1185
01:18:04.520 --> 01:18:05.560
A lie.

1186
01:18:06.440 --> 01:18:08.440
Barça! Barça!

1187
01:18:08.520 --> 01:18:12.080
[anchor, in Spanish] Mr. Gaspart,
this must be a very happy day for you.

1188
01:18:12.160 --> 01:18:14.200
Your first as president of Barcelona.

1189
01:18:14.280 --> 01:18:18.440
But I'm going to sour it a little
because I'm going to ask about Luís Figo.

1190
01:18:18.520 --> 01:18:19.600
What do you have to say?

1191
01:18:20.120 --> 01:18:25.760
[in Spanish] From what I know, Luís Figo
has signed a contract with Real Madrid.

1192
01:18:26.600 --> 01:18:30.560
If that's true, if Luís Figo
has actually signed this contract,

1193
01:18:30.640 --> 01:18:33.200
then there's nothing to be done,

1194
01:18:33.840 --> 01:18:36.920
and unfortunately,
Figo may now be a Real Madrid player.

1195
01:18:37.000 --> 01:18:38.000
But at what price?

1196
01:18:41.960 --> 01:18:43.960
[Spanish reporter 1]
He's the man of the hour,

1197
01:18:44.040 --> 01:18:46.640
the Portuguese star Luís Figo…

1198
01:18:46.720 --> 01:18:49.640
[Spanish reporter 2] Luís Figo
is already in Madrid, and this evening

1199
01:18:49.720 --> 01:18:52.400
he'll be presented at Bernabéu…

1200
01:18:52.480 --> 01:18:56.440
[French reporter] He's signing a six-year
contract with archenemies Real Madrid…

1201
01:18:56.520 --> 01:18:59.760
[Portuguese reporter] …making it
the most expensive transfer in the world.

1202
01:18:59.840 --> 01:19:02.160
[Spanish reporter 3]
Money is a powerful figure,

1203
01:19:02.240 --> 01:19:04.040
capable of making possible

1204
01:19:04.120 --> 01:19:05.400
what seemed impossible.

1205
01:19:17.320 --> 01:19:20.280
[Figo] We hadn't even
returned to Barcelona after the Euros

1206
01:19:21.720 --> 01:19:23.200
because I'd gone on holiday,

1207
01:19:23.800 --> 01:19:25.080
and I never went back.

1208
01:19:25.920 --> 01:19:28.320
From there,
I went straight to the presentation.

1209
01:19:34.000 --> 01:19:36.720
[Spanish paparazzo 1]
Don't worry about it.

1210
01:19:36.800 --> 01:19:39.600
Of course I'm gonna go for it.

1211
01:19:40.440 --> 01:19:42.040
[paparazzo 2 curses in Spanish]

1212
01:19:43.000 --> 01:19:46.160
-[paparazzo 2] Go for it. Get the picture!
-[car horn honks]

1213
01:19:46.240 --> 01:19:48.240
[car accelerates]

1214
01:19:51.360 --> 01:19:53.720
[paparazzo 2]
We're the only ones following him.

1215
01:19:56.680 --> 01:19:59.880
[paparazzo 1] Screw this guy.
Get right next to him.

1216
01:19:59.960 --> 01:20:02.840
Just get right next to him.
Fuck this dickhead.

1217
01:20:02.920 --> 01:20:05.200
-He can go fuck himself.
-[paparazzo 2] Shit.

1218
01:20:05.280 --> 01:20:07.600
[paparazzo 1 swears profusely]

1219
01:20:21.640 --> 01:20:23.080
[Díaz] It was a small room.

1220
01:20:23.920 --> 01:20:24.840
It was really hot.

1221
01:20:24.920 --> 01:20:28.120
People running after him all day,
"Where's Figo?" Chasing after him.

1222
01:20:33.960 --> 01:20:36.240
And suddenly,
the scene in that small room was

1223
01:20:36.320 --> 01:20:39.280
Di Stéfano and Florentino Pérez,
with a shirt.

1224
01:20:39.360 --> 01:20:40.640
Di Stéfano was happy.

1225
01:20:41.880 --> 01:20:43.280
Florentino was glowing.

1226
01:20:43.360 --> 01:20:44.280
But Figo…

1227
01:20:50.040 --> 01:20:52.040
[unheard dialogue]

1228
01:21:03.480 --> 01:21:05.480
[unheard dialogue]

1229
01:21:11.160 --> 01:21:12.480
[in Spanish] Good evening,

1230
01:21:13.360 --> 01:21:14.320
everyone.

1231
01:21:16.360 --> 01:21:19.040
For me, it's hugely satisfying

1232
01:21:20.080 --> 01:21:22.920
to be in this wonderful place,

1233
01:21:23.000 --> 01:21:27.040
surrounded by so many trophies
won by Real Madrid throughout its history.

1234
01:21:28.040 --> 01:21:30.800
And to be here
with our honorary president,

1235
01:21:30.880 --> 01:21:32.360
Don Alfredo Di Stéfano.

1236
01:21:33.120 --> 01:21:37.080
Above all, I'm here to present to you,
and this is my first act of presentation,

1237
01:21:37.680 --> 01:21:41.600
one of the best players
in the world, Luís Figo.

1238
01:21:45.200 --> 01:21:50.600
Luís, I'd like to welcome you to the club

1239
01:21:51.120 --> 01:21:52.800
that will become your home.

1240
01:21:52.880 --> 01:21:56.720
You'll be delighted
to have made this decision,

1241
01:21:57.320 --> 01:22:01.280
and the fans will no doubt love you…

1242
01:22:01.360 --> 01:22:04.520
-[journalists talking in Spanish]
-[people shushing loudly]

1243
01:22:05.080 --> 01:22:08.960
…just as the board of directors love you.

1244
01:22:09.040 --> 01:22:10.480
Thank you very much, Luís.

1245
01:22:10.560 --> 01:22:12.200
[applause erupts]

1246
01:22:27.600 --> 01:22:30.120
[Figo] In a moment like this,
you think so many things.

1247
01:22:30.200 --> 01:22:32.320
So many things
are going through your head.

1248
01:22:36.560 --> 01:22:38.720
Maybe you shut out how you really feel.

1249
01:22:51.240 --> 01:22:54.840
To make that decision
and suddenly be presented in Madrid,

1250
01:22:56.400 --> 01:22:58.120
built up a well of emotions.

1251
01:23:05.560 --> 01:23:08.600
I wasn't in the frame of mind
to express my happiness.

1252
01:23:11.240 --> 01:23:12.880
I was there but wasn't there.

1253
01:23:34.480 --> 01:23:36.560
So many things happened all at once,

1254
01:23:38.680 --> 01:23:39.800
and they can make you…

1255
01:23:41.760 --> 01:23:42.600
um…

1256
01:23:45.680 --> 01:23:47.040
Not crush you, but…

1257
01:23:48.720 --> 01:23:49.760
they affect you.

1258
01:24:01.520 --> 01:24:03.760
I'M HERE

1259
01:24:03.840 --> 01:24:07.600
FIGO, TRAITOR!

1260
01:24:11.280 --> 01:24:13.440
[in Spanish] We wish him all the best,

1261
01:24:14.320 --> 01:24:17.240
especially those of us
who know him and love him.

1262
01:24:17.320 --> 01:24:20.400
If it's his-- it's his decision,

1263
01:24:21.560 --> 01:24:24.040
then I think it's perfect
because it's his life.

1264
01:24:25.240 --> 01:24:29.200
We lose an irreplaceable player
with immense talent.

1265
01:24:30.160 --> 01:24:31.680
We just wish him all the best.

1266
01:24:32.840 --> 01:24:34.720
It made me sad, I'm not gonna lie.

1267
01:24:35.240 --> 01:24:39.120
I'd have preferred Luís to stay with me,
not just on the pitch but off it too,

1268
01:24:39.200 --> 01:24:40.480
in the dressing room.

1269
01:24:41.880 --> 01:24:44.440
I know we spoke
in the following day or days,

1270
01:24:45.760 --> 01:24:48.480
and I wished him luck
and told him that I'd miss him,

1271
01:24:48.560 --> 01:24:50.600
and I really did, for many years,

1272
01:24:50.680 --> 01:24:51.760
and that's that.

1273
01:24:54.920 --> 01:24:57.360
[dramatic electronic music plays]

1274
01:25:07.040 --> 01:25:08.480
I can't speak for Barça,

1275
01:25:09.000 --> 01:25:12.040
but I felt like I'd been stabbed
like a bull in a ring.

1276
01:25:12.120 --> 01:25:13.440
It tore me apart.

1277
01:25:15.680 --> 01:25:18.520
[in Spanish] Figo is leaving Barça
because he wants to.

1278
01:25:19.040 --> 01:25:21.160
I hope he doesn't look for any excuses.

1279
01:25:21.240 --> 01:25:22.200
He should be brave.

1280
01:25:22.720 --> 01:25:25.280
And he should say
that money is everything in life.

1281
01:25:26.520 --> 01:25:28.280
I understand that, and that's fair.

1282
01:25:28.840 --> 01:25:30.120
As long as he says it

1283
01:25:30.200 --> 01:25:34.080
and is not ashamed
for wanting more and more and more.

1284
01:25:34.920 --> 01:25:36.640
Joan Gaspart will not forget this.

1285
01:25:36.720 --> 01:25:37.720
[man speaking in Spanish]

1286
01:25:39.200 --> 01:25:40.800
[man, in Spanish] Cheer up, Figo!

1287
01:25:40.880 --> 01:25:43.040
You'll be better off here
than in Barcelona!

1288
01:25:44.760 --> 01:25:46.800
This is the best city in the world.

1289
01:25:48.280 --> 01:25:49.120
Champion!

1290
01:25:50.280 --> 01:25:52.520
Good luck! All the best for your future.

1291
01:25:53.160 --> 01:25:54.760
[photographer, in Spanish] Let's see!

1292
01:25:55.400 --> 01:25:56.240
Good morning.

1293
01:25:56.320 --> 01:26:00.000
[Figo, in Spanish]
I always respect other people's opinions,

1294
01:26:02.000 --> 01:26:05.520
so people have to respect my decision
whether they like it or not.

1295
01:26:06.720 --> 01:26:10.240
Uh, they call me a traitor but, um,

1296
01:26:11.120 --> 01:26:15.000
maybe the people who call me a traitor
are the ones who betrayed me.

1297
01:26:16.760 --> 01:26:19.720
I'm focused on being here

1298
01:26:19.800 --> 01:26:24.440
and doing the best I can
to represent this club.

1299
01:26:27.240 --> 01:26:31.160
3 MONTHS LATER

1300
01:26:33.080 --> 01:26:36.040
[anchor, in Spanish] All these seats
that you're currently seeing

1301
01:26:36.120 --> 01:26:37.920
are going to be filled.

1302
01:26:38.000 --> 01:26:40.480
A hundred thousand people
will be at the Nou Camp.

1303
01:26:40.560 --> 01:26:41.760
It's sold out.

1304
01:26:41.840 --> 01:26:44.720
So it's Barça versus Real Madrid,

1305
01:26:44.800 --> 01:26:48.640
or maybe it's more appropriate
to say the game is really

1306
01:26:48.720 --> 01:26:50.320
Barça against Figo.

1307
01:26:53.280 --> 01:26:56.240
[Spanish journalist 1] Does Luís think
people in Barcelona will forgive him?

1308
01:26:57.640 --> 01:26:59.160
[Spanish journalist 2] All I'm saying

1309
01:27:00.480 --> 01:27:02.280
is they're going to boo Figo.

1310
01:27:02.360 --> 01:27:04.560
They'll boo him a lot
because of how he left.

1311
01:27:09.400 --> 01:27:12.360
[Spanish reporter 3] The Nou Camp
is wounded and ready to condemn

1312
01:27:12.440 --> 01:27:15.200
the man who left
for the place that hurts the fans most.

1313
01:27:18.960 --> 01:27:21.080
[Valdano] I don't think
Figo quite realized

1314
01:27:21.160 --> 01:27:23.280
the full scale
of what was about to happen.

1315
01:27:25.120 --> 01:27:30.400
Hatred from fans is directly proportional
to the love they feel for a player.

1316
01:27:33.160 --> 01:27:35.600
And Figo was adored in Barcelona.

1317
01:27:37.240 --> 01:27:39.240
[photographer speaking in Spanish]

1318
01:27:41.800 --> 01:27:44.560
[reporter, in Spanish]
600 reporters, 200 from abroad.

1319
01:27:44.640 --> 01:27:47.480
All of whom will bear witness
to Luís Figo's return to the Nou Camp.

1320
01:27:48.000 --> 01:27:50.640
[man, in Spanish] He doesn't realize
what he did to Barça fans.

1321
01:27:50.720 --> 01:27:53.640
But he's screwed
if he wants to play football tonight.

1322
01:27:53.720 --> 01:27:56.000
[in Spanish] We're not allowed
to throw anything.

1323
01:27:56.080 --> 01:27:59.560
But if I could,
I'd throw a rock at his head.

1324
01:27:59.640 --> 01:28:03.160
[in Spanish] Joan, you seem very tense,

1325
01:28:03.240 --> 01:28:06.000
while Florentino,
you seem completely relaxed.

1326
01:28:06.600 --> 01:28:08.880
[in Spanish] That's down
to our personalities.

1327
01:28:08.960 --> 01:28:11.920
You know that I take these games
very seriously

1328
01:28:12.000 --> 01:28:13.200
and passionately

1329
01:28:13.280 --> 01:28:17.320
because we have to admit
this rivalry goes back a long way.

1330
01:28:17.400 --> 01:28:21.560
And, however much we have lunch together,
that's not going to change.

1331
01:28:22.160 --> 01:28:26.120
Well, there you have it.
What you see here is cordiality.

1332
01:28:26.200 --> 01:28:30.040
Let's see how things are
in 5 hours and 30 minutes.

1333
01:28:30.120 --> 01:28:32.200
[tense electronic music plays]

1334
01:28:36.680 --> 01:28:37.760
[indistinct dialogue]

1335
01:28:43.760 --> 01:28:46.160
[in Portuguese]
"Traitor, Judas, mercenary."

1336
01:28:46.240 --> 01:28:49.480
These insults are the least
Figo can expect from Barça fans.

1337
01:28:49.560 --> 01:28:52.760
[in Spanish] Just a plea
that nothing serious happens.

1338
01:28:52.840 --> 01:28:55.480
[in Spanish] We speak about Figo
as if he's public enemy number one.

1339
01:28:55.560 --> 01:28:58.680
[in Spanish] No, sorry,
he's not a criminal, but he is a traitor!

1340
01:29:00.040 --> 01:29:02.920
[journalist, in Spanish]
Don't take a photo with the shirt.

1341
01:29:03.000 --> 01:29:05.040
Don't say, "I'm not leaving!"

1342
01:29:05.120 --> 01:29:07.360
[angrily] That's what
he shouldn't have done!

1343
01:29:07.440 --> 01:29:10.200
-[man laughing]
-[in Spanish] Figo, you son of a bitch!

1344
01:29:10.280 --> 01:29:12.200
[laughter continues]

1345
01:29:12.280 --> 01:29:15.120
Where's Figo? Where's Figo?

1346
01:29:15.200 --> 01:29:18.560
Figo? Where's Figo? Where's Figo?

1347
01:29:19.080 --> 01:29:20.400
Where's Figo?

1348
01:29:20.480 --> 01:29:22.480
You're a mercenary!

1349
01:29:22.560 --> 01:29:27.200
-[rider shouting expletives in Spanish]
-[men laughing]

1350
01:29:32.400 --> 01:29:35.440
[chanting, in Spanish] Figo, you bastard!
Your girlfriend is a whore!

1351
01:29:35.520 --> 01:29:38.120
Figo, you bastard!
Your girlfriend is a whore!

1352
01:29:38.640 --> 01:29:41.080
FIGO MERCENARY

1353
01:29:54.360 --> 01:29:57.160
[unheard dialogue]

1354
01:29:58.440 --> 01:30:00.880
[people chanting angrily]

1355
01:30:03.760 --> 01:30:05.760
[people whistling shrilly]

1356
01:30:22.440 --> 01:30:25.840
FIGO = TRAITOR, LIAR, AND MONEY-GRUBBER

1357
01:30:25.920 --> 01:30:29.320
FIGO, YOU WOULD SELL YOUR MOM
IF YOU KNEW WHO SHE WAS

1358
01:30:41.200 --> 01:30:43.200
[crowd cheering raucously]

1359
01:30:45.800 --> 01:30:49.280
To be honest, it was one of those games
that when I went out to warm up,

1360
01:30:49.360 --> 01:30:51.680
if the referee had said
he was cancelling the match,

1361
01:30:51.760 --> 01:30:53.040
I'd have been delighted.

1362
01:30:53.560 --> 01:30:55.040
NEW CURRENCY NOTE

1363
01:30:55.120 --> 01:30:57.560
[Spanish anchor] It's an intimidating
atmosphere at Nou Camp.

1364
01:30:57.640 --> 01:31:00.200
You can feel the tension in the stadium.

1365
01:31:04.120 --> 01:31:08.360
Obviously, because of the SPORT front page
and all of those things, people felt bad.

1366
01:31:08.440 --> 01:31:09.840
They felt hurt and deceived.

1367
01:31:11.560 --> 01:31:14.160
But at the end of the day,
people have to understand

1368
01:31:14.240 --> 01:31:16.720
that everyone has the right
to make their own choices,

1369
01:31:16.800 --> 01:31:19.320
but things went too far,
a line was crossed,

1370
01:31:19.400 --> 01:31:20.800
and what happened happened.

1371
01:31:22.640 --> 01:31:24.560
[cacophonous roar of crowd]

1372
01:31:26.760 --> 01:31:29.400
[Valdano] It was impossible
not to have been affected

1373
01:31:29.480 --> 01:31:31.160
when it came down to the football

1374
01:31:31.640 --> 01:31:33.040
because the atmosphere

1375
01:31:33.800 --> 01:31:34.720
was unbearable.

1376
01:31:36.040 --> 01:31:37.720
I've never seen anything like it.

1377
01:31:41.200 --> 01:31:44.400
[Barça fans, chanting in Spanish]
Figo, you should die!

1378
01:31:44.480 --> 01:31:45.480
[Barça fans roar angrily]

1379
01:31:45.560 --> 01:31:47.680
[commentator 1, in Spanish]
Listen to the welcome

1380
01:31:47.760 --> 01:31:49.720
the Madrid players are getting.

1381
01:31:51.720 --> 01:31:53.480
[commentator 2, in Spanish]
I can't remember

1382
01:31:53.560 --> 01:31:56.120
an atmosphere as rough as this one.

1383
01:31:57.080 --> 01:31:59.160
Watch out!

1384
01:31:59.240 --> 01:32:02.000
This could explode at any moment!

1385
01:32:02.080 --> 01:32:03.600
[Barça fans booing angrily]

1386
01:32:03.680 --> 01:32:05.760
[announcer] …Raúl, Figo…

1387
01:32:05.840 --> 01:32:07.840
[Barça fans roar aggressively]

1388
01:32:12.560 --> 01:32:15.360
[interviewer] Did anyone
suggest to Figo not to play that day?

1389
01:32:15.440 --> 01:32:16.280
No. [tutting]

1390
01:32:18.840 --> 01:32:22.080
Firstly, because we weren't in a position
to tell him what to do.

1391
01:32:22.160 --> 01:32:26.480
Secondly, everyone who knows Luís
knew he wouldn't listen anyway.

1392
01:32:29.720 --> 01:32:30.920
That would be cowardly.

1393
01:32:32.000 --> 01:32:33.240
That would be giving in.

1394
01:32:35.720 --> 01:32:38.520
That would be giving in
to the people that were attacking me.

1395
01:32:38.600 --> 01:32:40.000
[spectators roar]

1396
01:32:40.080 --> 01:32:43.560
[commentator 1] Figo is looking
quite serious. What a test this is!

1397
01:33:04.520 --> 01:33:10.680
[Barça fans, chanting]
Portuguese son of a bitch!

1398
01:33:13.160 --> 01:33:15.160
[crowd roars]

1399
01:33:17.480 --> 01:33:20.240
FIGO, TRAITOR
WELCOME TO HELL

1400
01:33:20.320 --> 01:33:23.280
[Barça fans, chanting] Figo, you bastard!
Your girlfriend is a whore!

1401
01:33:23.360 --> 01:33:26.080
Figo, you bastard!
Your girlfriend is a whore!

1402
01:33:28.040 --> 01:33:30.680
Figo, die already!

1403
01:33:45.400 --> 01:33:47.280
Son of a bitch!

1404
01:33:48.440 --> 01:33:50.520
Son of a bitch!

1405
01:33:51.160 --> 01:33:53.280
[commentator talking excitedly in Spanish]

1406
01:34:00.760 --> 01:34:03.920
-[air horns honking]
-[Barça fans chanting]

1407
01:34:06.360 --> 01:34:09.840
[commentator 1] There we go again
with fans throwing things.

1408
01:34:09.920 --> 01:34:11.920
[commentary continues]

1409
01:34:15.520 --> 01:34:16.720
[whistle blows]

1410
01:34:17.680 --> 01:34:20.360
[Portuguese commentator]
There goes the final whistle. Barça, 2-0.

1411
01:34:32.600 --> 01:34:34.240
[Figo] The fans reacted the way they did

1412
01:34:34.320 --> 01:34:37.120
because the press
really stirred things up.

1413
01:34:37.200 --> 01:34:40.680
YOU BETRAYED US

1414
01:34:40.760 --> 01:34:43.600
[Figo] It was no longer a question
of being angry at a transfer…

1415
01:34:47.640 --> 01:34:49.080
which I could understand.

1416
01:34:49.160 --> 01:34:52.360
It was a personal attack
and against my family.

1417
01:34:53.840 --> 01:34:55.520
So after that, I drew a line.

1418
01:34:56.040 --> 01:34:57.400
I've had it. It's over.

1419
01:35:07.600 --> 01:35:11.680
10,000 PESETAS
MERCENARY

1420
01:35:18.760 --> 01:35:23.720
-[melancholic piano plays]
-[fans, chanting] Figo! Figo! Figo! Figo!

1421
01:35:38.840 --> 01:35:41.040
[Figo] With all that happened at Madrid,

1422
01:35:41.120 --> 01:35:43.280
I can say with 100% conviction

1423
01:35:43.360 --> 01:35:45.720
that it was the right decision
to join the club.

1424
01:35:48.320 --> 01:35:51.000
[speaking French]

1425
01:35:56.440 --> 01:35:58.360
[Figo] In 2000, I won the Ballon d'Or.

1426
01:35:59.760 --> 01:36:01.680
To win that trophy was crazy.

1427
01:36:03.400 --> 01:36:05.400
[commentator speaking in Spanish]

1428
01:36:10.480 --> 01:36:12.480
[commentator shouting enthusiastically]

1429
01:36:19.520 --> 01:36:22.240
[Figo] In my first year,
with all the pressure I was under,

1430
01:36:22.320 --> 01:36:23.240
we won the league.

1431
01:36:33.440 --> 01:36:35.400
Second year, we won the Champions League.

1432
01:36:36.320 --> 01:36:38.320
[piano music continues]

1433
01:36:52.040 --> 01:36:53.200
[Figo] We won everything.

1434
01:36:55.360 --> 01:36:58.720
I don't know if I changed the rivalry.
It will always be there.

1435
01:36:58.800 --> 01:37:01.200
But did anything change
within Spanish football?

1436
01:37:01.280 --> 01:37:02.440
Yes, it did.

1437
01:37:02.520 --> 01:37:05.400
Because it was the first major transfer
in world football.

1438
01:37:07.240 --> 01:37:09.120
It also changed the cycle of victory.

1439
01:37:12.800 --> 01:37:14.520
Was that down to my move?

1440
01:37:14.600 --> 01:37:15.760
I don't know.

1441
01:37:16.400 --> 01:37:18.840
But the record shows
that the cycle changed,

1442
01:37:20.840 --> 01:37:24.400
because Barcelona then went five years
without winning anything.

1443
01:37:32.240 --> 01:37:34.240
[speaking Spanish]

1444
01:37:37.600 --> 01:37:39.560
[Gaspart] Barça lost their best player,

1445
01:37:39.640 --> 01:37:43.560
and Madrid suddenly had the best player
in Spanish football at that time.

1446
01:37:45.760 --> 01:37:48.160
[Spanish reporter] Have you forgotten
the whole Figo thing?

1447
01:37:48.240 --> 01:37:50.560
-[Spanish] We've not discussed the matter.
-[Pérez laughs]

1448
01:37:50.640 --> 01:37:52.680
[indistinct dialogue]

1449
01:37:52.760 --> 01:37:56.080
[Gaspart] I admire Florentino Pérez
tremendously as a person.

1450
01:37:57.320 --> 01:37:59.240
But as president of Real Madrid,

1451
01:38:00.760 --> 01:38:02.280
he's my sworn enemy

1452
01:38:02.360 --> 01:38:05.480
and a man who played a dirty trick
that left me with a mandate

1453
01:38:05.560 --> 01:38:07.240
that ended very badly.

1454
01:38:09.080 --> 01:38:15.920
JOAN GASPART RESIGNED
AS PRESIDENT OF FC BARCELONA IN 2003

1455
01:38:16.000 --> 01:38:20.840
[spectators, chanting in Spanish]
Gaspart out! Gaspart out! Gaspart out!

1456
01:38:23.320 --> 01:38:25.360
[Gaspart] He's still
the president of Madrid,

1457
01:38:26.040 --> 01:38:29.200
and I was one of the worst presidents
in Barça's history.

1458
01:38:31.520 --> 01:38:32.480
[man 1] Florentino!

1459
01:38:33.480 --> 01:38:35.280
[man 2] Floren! Florentino!

1460
01:38:37.800 --> 01:38:43.480
LUÍS FIGO WAS THE FIRST
OF FLORENTINO PÉREZ'S "GALÁCTICOS"

1461
01:38:48.760 --> 01:38:53.000
[Pérez] I think we made a bold statement
and said, "Let's do something big."

1462
01:38:58.640 --> 01:39:01.400
And then I think
that the world of football changed,

1463
01:39:01.480 --> 01:39:02.880
without a shadow of a doubt.

1464
01:39:03.680 --> 01:39:06.240
PÉREZ IS STILL PRESIDENT OF REAL MADRID

1465
01:39:06.320 --> 01:39:10.640
AND IS NOW SPEARHEADING
THE EUROPEAN SUPER LEAGUE

1466
01:39:12.400 --> 01:39:15.400
Whenever I see him,
I say, "Figo, it all started with you!"

1467
01:39:17.640 --> 01:39:22.480
[muffled dialogue]

1468
01:39:22.560 --> 01:39:26.120
[Futre] I'll never forget the conversation
I had with Luís. I told him,

1469
01:39:26.200 --> 01:39:28.320
"I've been retired for a year and a half."

1470
01:39:30.800 --> 01:39:34.000
"The Portuguese Federation
still haven't invited me to a game."

1471
01:39:35.680 --> 01:39:37.760
"Not even to a friendly. Nothing."

1472
01:39:39.600 --> 01:39:42.520
"Why am I telling you this?
Because at the end of the day,

1473
01:39:42.600 --> 01:39:46.800
what counts isn't the medals,
the Ballon d'Or, the Bola de Prata."

1474
01:39:46.880 --> 01:39:48.840
"It isn't even the Champions League."

1475
01:39:48.920 --> 01:39:51.640
"At the end of the day,
what's important is the money."

1476
01:39:51.720 --> 01:39:53.040
"The money that you make."

1477
01:39:55.600 --> 01:39:59.520
PAULO FUTRE MADE 1.5 MILLION EUROS
FOR HIS ROLE IN THE TRANSFER

1478
01:39:59.600 --> 01:40:06.120
JOSÉ VEIGA MADE 3 MILLION EUROS
FOR HIS PART

1479
01:40:15.680 --> 01:40:18.120
[Guardiola] If we knew
how to find happiness, we'd go find it.

1480
01:40:18.200 --> 01:40:19.360
We'd go straight there.

1481
01:40:19.440 --> 01:40:22.960
You make a decision because you feel
it's best for you and your family.

1482
01:40:23.040 --> 01:40:24.800
Who's anyone to tell you otherwise?

1483
01:40:27.080 --> 01:40:29.120
[crowd cheers enthusiastically]

1484
01:40:30.840 --> 01:40:33.120
Would I have liked him to stay? Of course.

1485
01:40:33.200 --> 01:40:35.360
Not just me
but a lot of people at the club,

1486
01:40:35.440 --> 01:40:37.840
in Barcelona and all over Catalonia.

1487
01:40:37.920 --> 01:40:40.720
Well, he chose to leave.
I wished him luck.

1488
01:40:40.800 --> 01:40:43.400
I know he was happy,
and that's all that matters.

1489
01:40:45.880 --> 01:40:47.360
BETWEEN 2008 AND 2012,

1490
01:40:47.440 --> 01:40:51.800
PEP GUARDIOLA WENT ON TO BECOME
BARCELONA'S MOST SUCCESSFUL COACH EVER

1491
01:40:56.440 --> 01:40:59.800
[Figo] If you were to ask me now
who I'd prefer to be more successful,

1492
01:40:59.880 --> 01:41:00.840
I'd say Madrid.

1493
01:41:01.960 --> 01:41:04.200
[English commentator] Zidane. Makélélé!

1494
01:41:04.960 --> 01:41:07.440
[shouting] It's come for Figo!

1495
01:41:08.120 --> 01:41:11.480
Luís Figo breaks Barcelona hearts

1496
01:41:11.560 --> 01:41:13.360
all over again!

1497
01:41:13.440 --> 01:41:16.440
LUÍS FIGO PLAYED
FOR REAL MADRID UNTIL 2005

1498
01:41:16.520 --> 01:41:21.040
HE STILL LIVES IN MADRID WITH HIS FAMILY

1499
01:41:21.120 --> 01:41:26.400
CATALONIA DOESN'T FORGET. JUDA$!!

1500
01:41:28.840 --> 01:41:31.600
[Figo] Throughout my career
I've made a lot of mistakes.

1501
01:41:35.680 --> 01:41:38.440
That's normal.
I'm not perfect, and I don't want to be.

1502
01:41:43.160 --> 01:41:45.520
But I didn't make those mistakes
to hurt anyone.

1503
01:41:48.240 --> 01:41:51.480
Maybe I hurt myself with a lot of them
because I couldn't say no.

1504
01:41:52.640 --> 01:41:53.720
Uh…

1505
01:41:54.440 --> 01:41:58.120
But I try not to have regrets
because I don't think they're of any use.

1506
01:42:06.240 --> 01:42:09.000
["Hala Madrid!"
by José de Aguilar plays quietly]

1507
01:42:13.080 --> 01:42:14.760
[music becoming gradually louder]

1508
01:42:20.760 --> 01:42:21.720
[music stops]
